    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/308": {
      "title": "Director of Philanthropy",
      "description": "Category: University Advancement JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States As Austin Peay State University approaches its centennial, we're seeking a Director of Philanthropy for an area unit fundraiser. The Director of Philanthropy’s primary responsibility will be the identification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship of major gift prospects capable of gifts in the $25,000 and up range. As Austin Peay State University approaches its centennial, we're seeking a Director of Philanthropy for the Division of Student Affairs. As institutional priorities evolve, this position may also be assigned additional fundraising responsibilities in support of the university’s overall philanthropic goals. The Director of Philanthropy’s primary responsibility will be the identification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship of major gift prospects capable of gifts in the $25,000 and up range. Primary Duties and Responsibilities As Austin Peay State University approaches its centennial, we're seeking a Director of Philanthropy for the Division of Student Affairs. As institutional priorities evolve, this position may also be assigned additional fundraising responsibilities in support of the university’s overall philanthropic goals. The Director of Philanthropy’s primary responsibility will be the identification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship of major gift prospects capable of gifts in the $25,000 and up range. Fundraising Management (70%): Work with the area leadership to identify and define priority needs to be funded through external support. Responsible for raising major gifts for the area unit’s priorities through pledges, outright gifts, or deferred gifts. Plan and execute a development plan, which includes identification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship of major gift donors ($10,000+), while working independently or collaboratively with volunteers. Manage a major gift prospect portfolio of between 85–100 qualified major gift prospects, including those top prospects requiring attention from the APSU President or area leadership. Execute 20+ contacts per month, with at least half being personal, direct contact. Serve as the main liaison between the Division of Alumni, Engagement and Philanthropy and units leadership, staff, and faculty. Document gifts and pledges and adhere to policies and procedures for accepting, recording, and acknowledging gifts. Coordinate donor engagement opportunities for the Vice President of Student Affairs. Assist in the coordination of sponsorship opportunities tied to student engagement initiatives, career readiness, and wellbeing. Coordinate donor experiences connected to key initiatives. Activities (30%): Work closely with the Division of Alumni, Engagement and Philanthropy, Athletics, and other internal stakeholders to maximize fundraising efforts through participation in alumni events, university events or meetings as deemed necessary for fundraising outcomes. Provide thoughtful, consistent and appropriate donor stewardship, including invitations to events and impact reports. Monitor and enter all activities in the CRM system in an accurate and timely manner. Coordinate a unit advisory council to include developing agendas and engagement experiences, managing follow up communication, and supporting the recruitment of new members. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Results-oriented with professional characteristics that include leadership, commitment to confidentiality, flexibility, team-orientation, attention to detail and sensitivity to the stewardship of long-term relationships. Experience cultivating and maintaining donors in a mission-driven organization. Ability to travel extensively (40% of the time), including overnight and occasional weekends. Minimum Requirements Bachelor’s degree and experience in fundraising, business development, marketing, sales or related field. Demonstrated ability to work with various stakeholders at all levels to achieve common goals and objectives Ability to work weekends, nights and travel when necessary Ideal candidate will have excellent written and verbal communication skills Candidate must show attention to detail and the ability to balance strategic and scheduled responsibilities. Physical Requirements Sedentary Work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/439": {
      "title": "Director of Athletics, Compliance",
      "description": "Category: Athletic Coaching, Training and Program Management JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Responsible to perform a variety of athletic compliance functions on a daily basis, including but not limited to, initial eligibility, official and unofficial visit approval, annual recruiting and education. Primary contact for bylaws 13,14, and 16. Monitor complimentary tickets, recruiting logs, and other processes. Compliance Monitoring and Enforcement: Conduct initial eligibility audits. Manage ticket requests for staff, student-athletes, and recruits. Oversee all aspects of bylaw 13-visit approvals, recruiting laws, and phone call monitoring. Conduct regular audits to ensure adherence to NCAA , and UAC regulations. Education and Training: Develop and direct a comprehensive program for educating, monitoring, reporting, and complying with all NCAA , UAC, and University rules and regulations. Educate coaches, student-athletes, and athletic department staff on NCAA rules and regulations. Develop and deliver training sessions and educational materials. Stay updated on changes to NCAA rules and communicate these changes to relevant stakeholders. Reporting and Documentation: Prepare and submit required NCAA and conference reports. Maintain comprehensive records of compliance activities and investigations. Ensure accurate and timely documentation of all compliance-related matters. Advisory Role: Serve as the primary advisor on compliance-related matters to the Athletic Director and other senior administrators. Provide guidance on compliance issues and develop strategies to address potential problems. Act as liaison with the NCAA , Financial Aid, and Registrar’s offices for compliance and scholarship issues. Interpret or secure interpretations for compliance with NCAA and UAC rules and procedures. Investigations and Violations: Investigate and report any potential violations of NCAA rules. Work with the NCAA and conference offices on investigations and reports. Develop corrective actions and compliance plans to address and prevent future violations. Policy Development: Develop and implement policies and procedures to ensure compliance with NCAA regulations. Review and update institutional compliance policies as necessary. Software and Systems Management: Serve as Manager of NCAA Compliance Software, departmental compliance software, and NCAA Initial-Eligibility Clearinghouse. Work closely with the faculty representative in the certification of eligibility and rules compliance issues. Recruiting and Financial Aid Oversight: Administer and oversee recruiting activities, Athletics Grants-in-Aid programs, eligibility certification for practice and competition, financial aid, NCAA squad lists, National Letters of Intent, and reporting of the same. Develop and produce educational materials, such as departmental and student-athlete compliance handbooks, and the annual NCAA rules brochure for alumni, boosters, and the general public. Waivers and Appeals: Compile, review, and submit requests for eligibility waivers and other requests for waivers and appeals related to NCAA rules. Attend the annual NCAA Compliance seminar and provide continuous updates for compliance with rules and procedures. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities In-depth understanding of NCAA regulations and compliance issues Strong organizational and administrative skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Detail-oriented with strong analytical skills. Proficiency in compliance software and database management. Minimum Requirements Minimum of a Bachelor’s degree Minimum of three (3) years of experience in NCAA compliance or a related field. The position may require evening and weekend hours. Occasional travel may be required for conferences and meetings. "
    },
