      "title": "Part-time Instructor (Pool) - Culinary Arts",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Austin Peay State University invites applications for adjunct opportunities in the Culinary Arts within the Associate of Applied Science Degree in Professional Services with a concentration in Culinary Arts or Recreation Administration. Position Summary Austin Peay State University invites applications for adjunct opportunities in the Culinary Arts within the Associates of Applied Science Degree in Professional Services with a concentration in Culinary Arts or Recreation Administration. Required Minimum Qualifications Earned Associates degree or higher in Culinary Arts or a related field from an accredited institution (related field may include hospitality administration [leadership], business, nutrition, food science, or others as approved by the Office of Academic Affairs) Demonstrated expertise in the Culinary Arts, including at least 3-5 years relevant work experience Particular experience in areas such as baking and pastries, international cuisine, gourmet foods, garde manger, cake decorating/pastry arts, dietary food preparation, and/or desserts. A background search will be required of the successful applicant Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience Primary duties and responsibilitie s The Culinary Arts Adjunct Instructor will teach no more than four (4) classes per semester This assignment may include evening and weekend hours, as well as teaching at all APSU campus locations. Candidates must possess a strong commitment to teaching and learning, working with diverse populations, and growing the university's mission and vision. In addition to teaching, the instructor must be ready and able to assist by working with other adjunct Culinary Arts Instructors and by promoting the program. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities A background in the areas of sanitation, nutrition, food production, baking, specialty cuisine, and catering. Effective communication skills "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/420": {
      "title": "Instructor of Management",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Austin Peay State University’s AACSB accredited College of Business invites applicants for an Instructor of Management with teaching interests in management and human resources to begin July 30, 2027. This is a three-year, renewable, nontenure, contract role to teach eight three-hour courses per year: four courses in Fall; four courses in Spring. Austin Peay State University is a comprehensive university committed to raising the educational attainment of the citizenry, developing programs and services that address regional needs, and providing collaborative opportunities that connect university expertise with private and public resources. Collectively, these endeavors contribute significantly to the intellectual, economic, social, physical, and cultural development of the region. Austin Peay State University is a comprehensive university committed to raising the educational attainment of the citizenry, developing programs and services that address regional needs, and providing collaborative opportunities that connect university expertise with private and public resources. Collectively, these endeavors contribute significantly to the intellectual, economic, social, physical, and cultural development of the region. APSU prepares students to be engaged and productive citizens, while recognizing that society and the marketplace require global awareness and continuous learning. APSU’s vision is to create a collaborative, integrative learning community, instilling in students’ habits of critical inquiry as they gain knowledge, skills and values for life and work in a global society. Austin Peay’s five core values, which set the tone for how the University works, are quality, innovation, collaboration, community and globalization. Primary Duties and Responsibilities This position requires active teaching related to the discipline. Knowledge Skills and Abilities •Possess knowledge, talents, and skills in management and human resources or a closely related discipline, and in multiple teaching methodologies including hybrid, flipped, and blended courses. The ideal candidate should be able to teach various management and human resources, including but not limited to Principles of Management, Human Resources Management, and Organization Behavior and Theory. •Demonstrate respect for the diverse learning needs of students. •Demonstrate the ability to develop and implement curriculum objectives and content for marketing and sales courses taught. •Demand and maintain high standards and expectations for all students. Physical Requirements Sedentary- Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Required Minimum Qualifications At minimum, candidates must possess one of the following: · Master’s Degree in Management with substantial work experience , or · Master’s Degree in Business with 18 graduate hours in Management with substantial work experience , or · Master's Degree in Business, Human Resources, or Organizational Behavior with 3+ years of professional experience in management or human resources that is current, substantial in terms of duration and level of responsibility, and clearly linked to the field While not required, the preferred candidate also will have business school teaching experience. · Teaching Philosophy Statement · A background search will be required of the successful candidate. Special Instructions to Applicants This position requires teaching a variety of management and human resources courses. In both your cover letter and CV, please make apparent the scope of the management or management-related roles you have occupied, along with key accomplishments. While this position does not require research, those candidates submitting publications on their CVs should include with each entry the publication ranking on the Australian Business Dean Council (ABDC) list. The ranking should be A*, A, B, or C. If the journal is not on the ABDC list, please note this. In addition, please include any significant consulting projects. If you have not completed your degree, please submit a letter from your committee chair or advisor with an anticipated completion date. The individual selected for this role must maintain qualifications to teach in the field through practice work such as consulting and/or publication of discipline-related academic research. You will not be able to attach your Letters of Recommendation, unofficial transcripts or any other supplemental document(s) nor modify your application after it has been submitted. Letters of Recommendation may be sent by hard copy to “Austin Peay State University, Human Resources Dept., PO Box 4507, Clarksville, TN 37044” with your name and desired position clearly indicated. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/431": {
      "title": "Instructor, Accounting",
      "description": "JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Austin Peay State University’s AACSB accredited College of Business, invites applicants for an Instructor of Accounting with teaching interests in undergraduate accounting courses to begin July 30, 2027. This is a three-year, renewable, nontenure, contract role to teach eight three-hour courses per year: four courses in Fall; four courses in Spring. Austin Peay State University’s AACSB-accredited College of Business invites applicants for an Instructor of Accounting with teaching interests in undergraduate accounting courses to begin in August 2027. This is a three-year, renewable, nontenu,re, contract role to teach eight three-hour courses per year: four courses in Fall; four courses in Spring. Primary Duties and Responsibilities This position requires active teaching related to the discipline. Knowledge Skills and Abilities Demonstrate respect for the diverse learning needs of students. Demonstrate the ability to develop and implement curriculum objectives and content for accounting courses taught. Demand and maintain high standards and expectations for all students Required Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Accounting with 3+ years of professional experience in accounting that is current, substantial in terms of duration and level of responsibility, and clearly linked to the field of accounting; or Master’s degree in Business with 18 graduate hours in accounting, with 3+ years of professional experience in accounting that is current, substantial in terms of duration and level of responsibility, and clearly linked to the field of accounting. Possess knowledge, talents, and skills in accounting, and in multiple teaching methodologies, including hybrid, flipped, and blended courses. The ideal candidate should be able to teach various accounting courses, including but not limited to Principles of Accounting I & II, Intermediate Accounting, and Cost Accounting. While not required, the preferred candidate will also have business school teaching experience. Physical Requirements Sedentary- Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Special Instructions This position requires teaching of accounting courses. In both your cover letter and CV, please make apparent the scope of the accounting business-related roles you have occupied, along with key accomplishments. While this position does not require research, those candidates submitting publications on their CVs should include with each entry the publication ranking on the Australian Business Dean Council (ABDC) list. The ranking should be A*, A, B, or C. If the journal is not on the ABDC list, please note this. In addition, please include any significant consulting projects. If you have not completed your degree, please submit a letter from your committee chair or advisor with an anticipated completion date. The individual selected for this role must maintain qualifications to teach in the field through practice work such as consulting and/or publication of discipline-related academic research. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/434": {
      "title": "Field Technician, Southeastern Grassland Initiatives",
      "description": "Category: Academic Program Management and Instructional Services JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: TN, United States Grassland loss is the greatest conservation issue facing eastern North American biodiversity. Our precious Southeastern grasslands have suffered immeasurable losses, and the species that depend on them are fading fast. Many of the grasslands that persisted over the past 200 years have disappeared over the past quarter-century. What will the next 25 years bring? If we want to reverse the tide of grassland biodiversity loss, our response must be rapid and unparalleled in magnitude. This immensely complex and ambitious challenge will take hard work, passion, and creativity. Are you ready to join the Southeastern Grasslands Institute’s team? Grassland loss is the greatest conservation issue facing eastern North American biodiversity. Our precious Southeastern grasslands have suffered immeasurable losses, and the species that depend on them are fading fast. Many of the grasslands that persisted over the past 200 years have disappeared over the past quarter-century. What will the next 25 years bring? If we want to reverse the tide of grassland biodiversity loss, our response must be rapid and unparalleled in magnitude. This immensely complex and ambitious challenge will take hard work, passion, and creativity. Are you ready to join the Southeastern Grasslands Institute’s team? Austin Peay State University’s (APSU) Southeastern Grasslands Institute (SGI) invites applications for a Field Technician position based in Clarksville, TN . The Field Technician will be responsible for carrying out restoration and land management work at a diverse array of national parks across the Southern and Eastern US. There may also be some limited opportunities to assist with vegetation monitoring. The Field Technician will travel extensively throughout the year, typically working an 8-day-on/6-day-off hitch schedule, with overnight stays and travel expenses covered by grant funds. Up to 90% of the time will be spent in the field. The Field Technician will receive daily direction from a Lead Field Technician and directly report to SGI’s Interior Plateau Grasslands Coordinator. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Implement grassland restoration and reconstruction projects in national parks across the Southern and Eastern US (e.g., invasive species management, treating woody encroachment, site preparation, and planting of restoration seed mixes). Plan daily fieldwork activities with the Lead Field Technician. Communicate project updates and needs with the Lead Field Technician. Assist in gathering written, photographic, and GIS data for each project location. Assist in writing and editing management plans for project locations. Read relevant materials and protocols. Participate in regular team meetings and SGI staff meetings. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of grassland plant species and community types of the Southeastern and/or Mid-Atlantic United States. Knowledge of grassland restoration and reconstruction practices. Knowledge of invasive species management. Ability to learn quickly and adapt to challenges. Ability to work as part of a team. Physical Requirements Ability to work a non-standard schedule, such as working 8 days on followed by 6 days off, beginning work at 5 am to avoid heat-related issues, or occasionally working late hours on time-sensitive needs. Must have a valid driver’s license and experience driving a wide variety of vehicles and ATVs, including 4WD. Must be able to hike over rugged terrain in a variety of landscapes (grasslands, wetlands, rugged hills, slopes, etc.) Willingness and ability to work in harsh, ever-changing environmental conditions, including hot temperatures, buggy conditions, and rain. Must be able to lift 50 pounds. Required Minimum Qualifications Experience in grassland restoration and/or land management strongly preferred. Comes prepared with a good attitude and willingness to learn. Must have excellent organizational and task-management skills. Must have excellent communication and interpersonal skills, and the ability to communicate and work effectively with a wide variety of people. Strong commitment to ensuring that diversity and inclusion are considered throughout all aspects of the program. Must be flexible with travel and work schedules. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/436": {
      "title": "Part-Time Receptionist",
      "description": "JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Division of Student Affairs at Austin Peay State University is committed to creating a welcoming, student-centered environment that supports student success, engagement, wellbeing, and belonging. Student Affairs team members contribute to this mission by providing responsive service, fostering positive relationships, and supporting the programs, services, and operations that enhance the student experience. The Part-Time Receptionist serves as a welcoming and professional first point of contact for students, families, employees, campus partners, and visitors. The position provides front office coverage, customer service, and routine clerical support to assist with the efficient day-to-day operation of the Division Office. The position performs established front desk and clerical functions under the direction of designated staff. Part-Time- 20 hours per week. Characteristics of a successful candidate: Demonstrate sincere enjoyment from working with students and colleagues. Motivation to create a caring and welcoming environment. Integrity, kindness, creativity, and decisiveness. Ability to serve with agility; important to lead, listen, and serve with empathy. A commitment to practicing open communication and inspiring trust. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced campus environment. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Front Office Support Serve as a welcoming, courteous, and professional first point of contact for students, families, employees, visitors, and other individuals seeking assistance from the office. Greet visitors and determine the nature of their visit, providing general assistance or directing them to the appropriate staff member, department, or campus resource. Answer incoming telephone calls and respond to routine inquiries using established information, procedures, and resources. Route telephone calls, messages, and requests to the appropriate staff member in a timely manner. Monitor the front desk and reception area and help maintain a professional, organized, and welcoming environment. Assist visitors with general information regarding office services, programs, appointments, events, and university resources. Receive and appropriately distribute mail, packages, deliveries, and other materials. Assist with visitor check-in and appointment notification. Maintain awareness of scheduled division office activities, meetings, programs, and events in order to provide accurate general information. Provide consistent front desk coverage during assigned work hours and communicate promptly with the supervisor regarding scheduling or coverage concerns. Maintain appropriate confidentiality and discretion when interacting with students, employees, and visitors. Department and Division Contribute to a welcoming, student-centered, professional, and service-oriented Division Office environment. Establish and maintain positive working relationships with students, colleagues, campus partners, and visitors. Engage in appropriate training and professional development necessary to perform assigned responsibilities effectively. Perform other duties as assigned that are consistent with the scope and purpose of the Part-Time Front Desk Support position. Required Skills and Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent. Experience providing customer service, reception, clerical, office or related support. Ability to communicate professionally and effectively with a variety of individuals. Basic computer proficiency, including the ability to use Microsoft office, and other standard office technology. Ability to maintain confidentiality and appropriately handle sensitive information. Ability to perform assigned responsibilities with reliability and attention to detail. Effective oral and written communication skills. Preferred Skills and Qualifications : Complementing the required skills and qualifications: Associate degree or a minimum of 60 completed college credit hours, and at least two years of related customer service, reception, clerical, or office support experience. Previous experience working in a college or university, educational setting, customer service environment, reception area, or professional office. Experience working directly with students, customers, clients, or the public. Experience performing routine data entry, recordkeeping, filing, or general office support. Demonstrated experience working successfully in a team-oriented environment. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/435": {
      "title": "Communication Specialist, College of Business",
      "description": "Category: Communications, Marketing, and Events JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Communication Specialist supports the College of Business’s communications and external engagement strategy by developing and implementing compelling content that communicates the College’s accomplishments, activities, people, programs, partnerships, and impact to internal and external audiences. Working under the direction of the Director of Strategic Partnerships and External Relations, the Communication Specialist serves as a primary producer of the College’s written, digital, social media, and visual communications. The position works closely with faculty, staff, students, alumni, business partners, and university communications personnel to identify and develop stories that advance the College’s strategic priorities and strengthen its visibility and reputation. The Communication Specialist supports the College of Business’s communications and external engagement strategy by developing and implementing compelling content that communicates the College’s accomplishments, activities, people, programs, partnerships, and impact to internal and external audiences. Working under the direction of the Director of Strategic Partnerships and External Relations, the Communication Specialist serves as a primary producer of the College’s written, digital, social media, and visual communications. The position works closely with faculty, staff, students, alumni, business partners, and university communications personnel to identify and develop stories that advance the College’s strategic priorities and strengthen its visibility and reputation. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Implement the College of Business’s communications strategy across appropriate print, digital, social media, and other communication channels. Develop and distribute press releases, media pitches, feature stories, announcements, newsletters, and other written communications highlighting the College’s faculty, students, programs, research, partnerships, events, and accomplishments. Manage and create content for the College’s social media channels, including developing editorial calendars, writing posts, creating visual content, monitoring engagement, and identifying opportunities to increase the College’s reach and visibility. Prepare and publish a quarterly College of Business newsletter for faculty, staff, students, and alumni. Develop graphics, promotional materials, presentations, digital content, and other visual communications consistent with University and College branding standards. Identify compelling stories and communications opportunities throughout the College by developing relationships with faculty, staff, students, alumni, and external partners. Coordinate with faculty and staff to gather information, photographs, quotes, and other materials necessary to develop accurate and compelling communications. Support communications related to the College’s external partnerships, Corporate Partners Program, student and faculty achievements, research, experiential learning, community engagement, and societal impact initiatives. Maintain and organize digital communications assets, including photographs, graphics, logos, templates, and other promotional materials. Coordinate with the university’s Office of Public Relations and Marketing and other university offices to ensure College communications are consistent with university policies, branding standards, and broader institutional communications. Monitor media coverage and social media engagement, and provide the Director with information on communications performance and opportunities. Assist with the development of College marketing campaigns, promotional materials, events, and special initiatives. Support the College’s website and other digital communications platforms by developing, updating, and coordinating content as appropriate. Assist in maintaining consistent messaging and visual identity across College communications and promotional materials. Support the Director in documenting and communicating the College’s educational, economic, and community impact. Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines while maintaining attention to detail and accuracy. Strong interpersonal and organizational skills and the ability to work effectively with faculty, staff, students, and external partners. Ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines while maintaining attention to detail and accuracy. Required Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in communications, public relations, journalism, marketing, graphic design, or a related field. Demonstrated experience developing written and visual content for professional, organizational, or institutional audiences. Excellent writing, editing, proofreading, and storytelling skills. Experience managing social media platforms and developing content for multiple audiences. Demonstrated graphic design skills and proficiency with commonly used graphic design and digital content creation tools. Familiarity with photography, video, web content management, email marketing, or other digital communications tools is desirable. Experience in higher education, business, nonprofit, or other mission-driven organizations is desirable. Physical Requirements Sedentary Work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/432": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Community Belonging",
      "description": "Category: Student Support, Advising, and Career Development JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Community Belonging Coordinator reports to the Director for Community Belonging and plays a vital role in advancing Austin Peay State University’s commitment to fostering a campus environment where every student feels connected, supported, and positioned for success. This role contributes to a comprehensive, student-centered strategy that strengthens students’ sense of belonging, engagement, and academic achievement. This position collaborates in a cross-divisional and cross-institutional approach to design, implement, and assess programs, services, and initiatives that enhance both social and academic belonging. This position supports holistic student experience by creating opportunities for connection, engagement, and success inside and outside of the classroom. The coordinator will serve with a student-centered approach that contributes to a caring and safe campus life environment that supports the holistic success of students. The Community Belonging Coordinator reports to the Director for Community Belonging and plays a vital role in advancing Austin Peay State University’s commitment to fostering a campus environment where every student feels connected, supported, and positioned for success. This role contributes to a comprehensive, student-centered strategy that strengthens students’ sense of belonging, engagement, and academic achievement Characteristics of a successful candidate: Demonstrates kindness, integrity, empathy, and sound judgment. Brings creativity and initiative to program development Motivation to create a caring and safe student experience. Ability to serve with agility; important to lead, listen, and serve with empathy. A commitment to practicing open communication and inspiring trust. Desire to collaborate with colleagues. Demonstrated sincere enjoyment from working with students. Key Focus Areas of the Role Strengthening student sense of belonging and connection. Enhancing academic belonging through collaboration and partnership with preexisting services. Creating integrated co-curricular experiences that support creating a campus that celebrates its uniqueness and student populations. Building campus partnerships that support student belonging to the APSU campus community. Responsibilities include: Community Building and Engagement Develop and coordinate programs and initiatives that strengthen students’ sense of belonging and connection to the university. Plan and implement campus events that foster engagement, community, and shared experiences. Create opportunities for peer connection, student involvement, and meaningful participation in campus life. Advise and support student organizations that contribute to campus engagement and belonging. Partner with campus departments to deliver collaborative programs that enhance student experience. Academic Belonging and Student Success Design and implement initiatives that support students’ academic engagement, persistence, and success. Collaborate with academic affairs, advising, and student support services to connect students with resources that promote achievement. Support programs that reinforce the connection between student engagement and academic outcomes. Utilize data and assessment to identify trends, inform strategies, and improve student success initiatives. Department and Division Maintain open communications with the Director for Community Belonging to share information and engage in issue-spotting and creative problem-solving to benefit the University community. Work with the Director to coordinate the management of resources of the Center. Under the direction of the Director, assist in the coordination and stewardship of departmental resources and budgets in alignment with university policies. Collaborate with campus and community partners to expand opportunities and support for students. Prepare reports and contribute to assessment efforts that demonstrate program effectiveness and student impact. Stay informed and educate the University community and stakeholders as needed regarding issues, trends, and regulations impacting student belongingness. Engage in ongoing professional development and remain informed of emerging trends in student engagement and success. Other duties as assigned. Required Skills and Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and related experience. Knowledge of best practices to support students in the university setting Demonstrated ability to develop and implement student programs and initiatives. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills . Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Experience using data to inform decision-making and program improvement. Preferred Skills and Qualifications : Complementing the required skills and qualifications: Master's degree, and at least 2 years of related experience as a full-time professional or graduate assistant. Experience supporting student engagement, retention, or success initiatives. Demonstrated ability to lead collaborative efforts across departments. Excellent presentation skills. Excellent writing skills. Experience with leading special initiatives, programs, and strategic planning. Physical Requirements: -Sedentary Work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/433": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Gov Outdoors",
      "description": "Category: Auxiliary Services JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Govs Outdoors Coordinator reports to the Assistant Director of Programs for University Recreation. This role provides coordination and has direct responsibility for all aspects of day-to-day Govs Outdoors programming and operations, including Rock Wall, Gear Rental, Low Ropes Challenge Course, Trip Program and Bike Repair program. This position supports Austin Peay State University’s commitment to fostering a vibrant campus life experience through safe, and well-managed recreational programs and facilities. The coordinator will be with a team that drives the strategy, vision, multidisciplinary and data-informed approach, and operational leadership to develop, inspire, and lead the care, standards, and wellbeing of student campus community. This position collaborates in a cross-Divisional and cross-institutional approach to advance operational excellence, student employment development, and risk management for best practices that align with university policies and strategic priorities. The coordinator serves with a student-centered approach that contributes to a caring and safe campus life environment, supporting the holistic success of students through leadership development, professional growth opportunities and high-quality recreational experiences. Characteristics of a successful candidate: Integrity, creativity, and decisiveness. Motivation to create an inclusive and safe student experience. Ability to serve with agility and manage multiple priorities. A commitment to practicing open communication and inspiring trust. Desire to collaborate with colleagues. A strong commitment to developing students holistically. Responsibilities include: Programming Responsible for the development, direction, and evaluation of a comprehensive outdoor recreation program that meets the needs of a variety of skills levels, abilities, and identities of the university community. Oversee all programs, events, and rentals within the Govs Outdoors program area, including Bouldering Competitions, Challenge Course and Rock Wall group requests, gear rentals, trip planning and facilitation. Enter and update all programs into the recreation management software system for registrations, sales, and reservations. In conjunction with the Assistant Director, create, identify, and assess program goals in support of University and Division missions and strategic plans. Monitor the industry trends for programming new and inclusive activities, and to inform future decisions. Assist with marketing as needed to promote Govs Outdoors Fiscal and Facility Operations In concert with the Assistant Director, oversee the Govs Outdoors budgets, including payroll, program/maintenance expenses, equipment repair and replacement, and tracking revenue. Forecast and monitor all wages, staffing, expenses and revenue to prepare future budget requests, including equipment replacement, in concert with the Assistant Director. Coordinate facility-use and requests with the University Recreation leadership team. Personnel and Leadership Development Recruit, hire, train, supervise, develop and evaluate Govs Outdoors staff of 5-10 student and non-student/part-time employees, including Govs Outdoors Adventure Leaders and Rock Wall Attendants Develop and implement in-services for Govs Outdoors staff following best practices with a strong emphasis on skill-development, transferable work skills, staff empowerment, inclusion and leadership. Enforces and communicates university and department policies with employees and patrons. Create, identify, and assess student learning outcomes in support of University and Division missions and strategic plans. Provide high-quality service within department guidelines in all interactions. Department and Division Collaborate with University Recreation staff to advance the departmental and divisional vision, mission, core values, and strategic plan Support the mission of University Recreation, Student Affairs, and APSU through active participation in departmental and campus-wide initiatives, and committees Remain competent and current through professional development and participation in professional organizations. Collaborate with APSU departments and community partners. Prepare timely and accurate reports. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Required Skills and Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Demonstrated experience in outdoor recreation programming or operations, including experience with outdoor adventure programs, challenge course facilitation, climbing programs, or leading group outdoor trips. Experience supervising, training, or providing leadership to student employees, part-time employees, volunteers, or program participants. Current Wilderness First Aid (WFA) certification, or ability to obtain certification within a specified period following employment. Demonstrated knowledge of safety practices and risk management principles associated with outdoor recreation programs and activities. Ability to effectively lead, develop, and work with individuals from a variety of backgrounds and experiences. Effective oral and written communication skills. Demonstrated organizational skills and ability to manage multiple priorities, deadlines, programs, and activities. Ability to work evenings and weekends as required to support Govs Outdoors programs, trips, and departmental or divisional activities. Valid driver’s license. Successful completion of a background check as required by the University. Preferred Skills and Qualifications: Master’s degree in Recreation Administration, Outdoor Recreation, Parks and Recreation, Higher Education, Student Affairs, Sport Management, or related field. Two or more years of professional or graduate-level experience in collegiate recreation, outdoor recreation, adventure education, or a related setting. Experience developing, coordinating, and assessing outdoor recreation programs, including adventure trips, climbing programs, challenge courses, equipment rental, or similar experiential programs. Experience recruiting, training, supervising, and developing student employees or part-time staff. Experience with outdoor recreation risk management, emergency action planning, incident response, and industry safety practices. Experience managing or assisting with program budgets, equipment inventories, purchasing, maintenance, and replacement planning. Experience using recreation management, registration, reservation, or point-of-sale software. Wilderness First Responder (WFR) certification. Wilderness First Aid Instructor certification. Climbing Wall Instructor certification or comparable climbing-related certification. Experience with paddling and other outdoor adventure activities. Physical Requirements -Sedentary Work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/430": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Communications",
      "description": "Category: Communications, Marketing, and Events JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Communications Coordinator reports to the Director of Student Affairs Assessment, Planning and Communications. The coordinator supports the development and execution of division communications and marketing initiatives through content creation, project coordination, digital communications and ongoing project tracking. Working collaboratively with the division communications team, division departments and university partners, this position helps ensure communications are timely, audience-centered, accurate and aligned with university and division standards. This role requires excellent communication and organizational skills and the ability to work independently and as part of a team. This position works within the Student Affairs communications team along with the Public Relations and Marketing teams in a fast-paced, dynamic environment to advance the vision of Student Affairs and support strategic goals. This role plays a key part in shaping how Student Affairs tells its story, engages students, and advances divisional priorities. The coordinator collaborates in a cross-divisional and cross-institutional approach to support the development, coordination and execution of strategic marketing and communications initiatives. The coordinator will take a student-centered approach to promote programs, services and resources that contribute to a supportive, engaging campus environment. Through intentional messaging, content creation, and brand alignment, this role helps enhance the student experience, increase awareness and support the holistic success of students. Characteristics of a successful candidate: Integrity, kindness, creativity, innovation, along with the capacity to inspire others. Ability to serve with agility; important to lead, listen, and serve with a high level of energy. A commitment to practicing open communication and inspiring trust. Desire to collaborate with colleagues and engage in a culture that rewards teamwork. Demonstrated sincere enjoyment from working in support of students. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Communications Production and Coordination Coordinate content development and production for assigned division communications and promotional projects. Develop and edit clear, engaging, and grammatically correct messaging for a variety of media including print collateral, digital assets, web pages, emails, etc. Assist with development of press releases. Assist with creating, preparing, scheduling and publishing assigned content on division social media accounts. Create and assist with multimedia assets. Effectively partner with Public Relations and Marketing, Govs Print, licensing, and other university communications teams. Ensure communications are consistent with university and division branding, voice, style, accessibility standards, procedures and guidelines. Assist with regular maintenance and updates of webpages. Assist with the development and implementation of communications campaigns that increase awareness of and engagement with Student Affairs programs, services and initiatives. Strengthen consistency and alignment of divisional messaging across platforms. Maintain project tracking information and compile monthly reports on communications team project volume, completed work and progress on team projects by established deadlines. Maintain project management documents, shared communication assets, files and related documentation to support project coordination and continuity. Evening and weekend work may be required at times. Department and Division Leadership Maintain regular communications with the director regarding project status, priorities, deadlines, emerging issues and opportunities to improve communications processes to fulfill goals. Openly collaborate and participate with Student Affairs communications team. Collaborate with division departments on communications requests. Effectively manage job related priorities and deadlines for deliverables. Participate in related professional organizations for continuing development and other professional development opportunities. Participate in and support division-wide activities, programs and initiatives as appropriate. Other projects and duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of marketing, public relations and communications principles, practices and techniques for engaging diverse audiences. Strong verbal and written communication, editing and proofreading skills with attention to detail. Knowledge of accessibility standards and their application to communication materials. Knowledge and application of Associated Press style and established university and division branding, style and communication guidelines. Proficiency with digital design and multimedia software. Ability to effectively use web technology, Adobe Creative Suite, Microsoft Office, Basecamp and other related software platforms. Ability to develop effective, audience-centered promotional materials and digital content. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment and adapt to shifting priorities. Ability to manage and meet competing priorities and deadlines. Ability to provide guidance and day-to-day direction to student interns or student assistants. Required Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in communications, public relations, marketing, or related field. At least one (1) year of relevant experience in communications, marketing, public relations, or related area. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in communications, public relations, marketing, or related field. At least two (2) years of progressively relevant experience in communications, public relations, marketing, or related area. Experience with communications in a higher education setting Physical Requirements Light Work: Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 10 pounds of force frequently, and/or a negligible amount of force constantly moving objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/429": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Sustainability",
      "description": "Category: Facilities Maintenance, Planning, Engineering, and Construction JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Sustainability Coordinator works collaboratively with administration, faculty, staff and students to develop, coordinate, and promote sustainability initiatives that reduce the University's environmental impact and advance environmental stewardship. This position reports to the Director, Campus Engagement & Sustainability and is responsible for educating the University community about sustainability, coordinating campus sustainability programming and activities, conducting research, supporting sustainability assessment and completing annual reporting. This position collaborates in a cross-divisional and cross-institutional approach to coordinate sustainability programs, projects and initiatives. The coordinator serves as a campus resource and liaison, connecting students, faculty, staff and community partners to advance sustainability goals and promote awareness of environmental issues and responsible practices. The coordinator will take a student-centered approach to engaging and advising students through educational programs, sustainability initiatives and leadership opportunities that promote environmental awareness and stewardship while contributing to a caring and supportive campus environment and the holistic success of students. Characteristics of a successful candidate: Integrity, kindness, creativity, and decisiveness. Motivation to create a caring and safe student experience. Ability to serve with agility; important to lead, listen, and serve with empathy. A commitment to practicing open communication and inspiring trust. Desire to collaborate with colleagues. Demonstrated sincere enjoyment from working with students. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Sustainability Programs and Initiatives Collaborate with students, faculty and staff across the residential and academic campus community to promote awareness and understanding of sustainability issues. Coordinate educational programs, presentations and initiatives related to energy and water conservation, waste minimization, recycling, sustainable building and landscape practices, alternative transportation, green procurement and other sustainability topics. Develop and coordinate sustainability programming and activities designed to engage the University community and promote environmental stewardship. Serve as a liaison among campus departments, student organizations, community partners and other stakeholders to support communication and resource coordination for sustainability programs and projects. Research sustainability practices and trends at peer and other institutions and recommend opportunities to strengthen University sustainability programs and practices. Research and identify grant opportunities and other potential funding sources to support and expand campus sustainability efforts. Coordinate recycling efforts across campus, including communication and coordination with appropriate outside vendors and contractors. Assessment, Reporting and Communications Coordinate and compile University data for the Association for the Advancement of Sustainability in Higher Education (AASHE) Sustainability Tracking, Assessment & Rating System (STARS). Coordinate the collection of information from campus departments and organizations and enter required data into the STARS reporting system for submission to AASHE. Assist with defining sustainability goals and tracking performance measures to assess program effectiveness and progress. Collect, organize and maintain sustainability data and documentation needed for assessment, reporting, and continuous improvement. Develop and maintain sustainability web content highlighting University sustainability initiatives, programs, events, educational opportunities, recycling information and related resources. Communicate sustainability accomplishments, opportunities and resources to the University community in collaboration with appropriate campus partners. Prepare reports, updates, and other materials related to university sustainability activities and progress. Student Engagement and Campus Collaboration Engage students in sustainability education, programming, leadership opportunities and campus initiatives. Work collaboratively with Student Government Association leadership on sustainability initiatives and related funding. Chair and coordinate Sustainable Campus Fee Committee meetings and support implementation of approved recommendations and initiatives. Promote student participation, leadership and enthusiasm in campus sustainability efforts. Collaborate with University departments and campus partners to advance sustainability initiatives and institutional priorities. Department and Division Leadership Maintain regular communication with the supervisor regarding project status, priorities, deadlines, emerging issues, and opportunities to strengthen sustainability initiatives. Effectively manage job-related priorities, projects, and deadlines for deliverables. Develop and maintain collaborative relationships with campus and community partners. Participate in related professional organizations and professional development opportunities. Participate in and support division-wide activities, programs and initiatives as appropriate. Represent the University and Division of Student Affairs professionally when interacting with internal and external stakeholders. Evening and weekend work may be required at times. Other projects and duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of sustainability principles, environmental stewardship, practices, and emerging trends. Knowledge of sustainability assessment, data collection, and reporting practices. Ability to develop, coordinate, and continuously improve innovative sustainability programs, initiatives, and educational activities. Strong interpersonal, organizational, written, and oral communication skills. Ability to establish and maintain collaborative, professional, and service-oriented relationships with students, faculty, staff, community partners, vendors, and external organizations. Ability to engage, guide, support, and motivate student leaders to participate in sustainability initiatives and programs. Ability to collect, organize, analyze and communicate sustainability-related data. Ability to conduct research and identify opportunities for program development and improvement. Ability to manage multiple projects, priorities, and deadlines. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment and adapt to shifting priorities. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and ability to learn and effectively use sustainability reporting and other related software platforms. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in sustainability, environmental science, environmental studies or related field. Related experience with sustainability, environmental programs, or initiatives. Demonstrated knowledge of sustainability practices and environmental stewardship. Strong written and oral communication skills . Demonstrated ability to collaborate with diverse stakeholders and manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Ability to analyze and assess data. Ability to work evenings and weekends as needed. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in sustainability, environmental science, environmental studies, higher education, public administration or related field. At least two (2) years of progressively relevant professional or graduate assistant experience in sustainability, environmental programming or related areas. Experience coordinating sustainability programs, special initiatives or strategic planning. Experience with sustainability assessment, reporting, or performance measures. Experience working with students or sustainability initiatives in a higher education setting. Physical Requirements Light Work: Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 10 pounds of force frequently, and/or a negligible amount of force constantly moving objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/280": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Residential Education",
      "description": "Category: Auxiliary Services JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Coordinator for Residential Education is a live-on professional staff member within the Office of Residence Life at Austin Peay State University and reports directly to the Director of Residence Life. This position provides strategic leadership for residential education by advancing a comprehensive, data-informed, and student-centered approach to programming and engagement within the residential community. The Coordinator supports the educational mission of Residence Life through the intentional development, implementation, and assessment of residential programming and student engagement initiatives. The Coordinator for Residential Education is a live-on professional staff member within the Office of Residence Life at Austin Peay State University and reports directly to the Director of Residence Life. This position provides strategic leadership for residential education by advancing a comprehensive, data-informed, and student-centered approach to programming and engagement within the residential community. The Coordinator supports the educational mission of Residence Life through the intentional development, implementation, and assessment of residential programming and student engagement initiatives. The Coordinator collaborates in a cross-Divisional and cross-institutional approach to enhance the residential experience and promote student success, belonging, and holistic development. This position provides oversight of the residential programming model and supervises Community Programming Directors (CPDs), ensuring alignment with departmental priorities and best practices in student engagement. The Coordinator also serves as a key liaison for Living-Learning Communities (LLCs) and other residential initiatives that support academic integration and student learning. This Coordinator contributes to the mission of the Division of Student Affairs by fostering engaging residential community environments, that support the personal, social, and leadership development of residential students. The Coordinator exercises independent judgment in managing programming initiatives, supervising student staff, and collaborating with campus partners to advance departmental goals and continuous improvement efforts Characteristics of a successful candidate: Integrity, kindness, creativity, and decisiveness, along with the capacity to inspire others. Motivation to create a thriving, engaged, and safe student experience. Ability to serve with agility; important to lead, listen, and serve with a high level of energy. A commitment to practicing open communication and inspiring trust. Desire to collaborate with colleagues and create a culture that rewards teamwork. Demonstrated sincere enjoyment from working with students. Responsibilities include: Residential Programming and Student Engagement Provide leadership for Residence Life programming initiatives that support the educational mission of the department and align with the Housing programming model. Develop and coordinate large-scale educational, cultural, social, and leadership programs that foster student engagement and community development within the residence halls. Provide direction and support to Community Programming Directors (CPDs) in the planning, implementation, and assessment of residential programming initiatives. Collaborate with faculty and campus partners to support Living-Learning Communities (LLCs) and other initiatives that enhance academic engagement within the residential environment. Student Staff Supervision and Development Supervise and mentor Community Programming Directors (CPDs) and other assigned student leaders. Provide ongoing training, guidance, and professional development opportunities to support student staff success. Facilitate regular meetings with student staff to support program planning, leadership development, and operational coordination. Evaluate student staff performance and provide developmental feedback to support growth and leadership capacity. Department and Division Leadership Maintain open communication with the Assistant Director of Residence Life to share information and engage in issue-spotting and creative problem-solving to benefit the residential community. Serve on Division and University committees, as assigned. Serve as a liaison between Residence Life and campus partners to enhance student success initiatives within residential communities. Collaborate with university departments and faculty to integrate academic and co-curricular experiences into the residential environment. Support divisional and institutional initiatives that promote student engagement, belonging, and success. Required Skills and Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Experience in residence life, student programming, or leadership development initiatives. Strong organizational, interpersonal, and written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to build and maintain effective relationships with students, faculty, and campus partners. Ability to collaborate effectively across departments to support student engagement and success. Demonstrated integrity, professionalism, and the ability to build trust with students and colleagues. Commitment to creating residential communities that promote belonging, engagement, and student success. Creativity and initiative in designing educational, social, and leadership development programming. Ability to balance multiple priorities in a dynamic environment while maintaining attention to detail and organizational effectiveness. Demonstrated interest in mentoring student leaders and supporting their personal and professional development. Ability to live on campus and work evenings and weekends as required. Preferred Skills and Qualifications Master’s degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, or a related field. Experience supervising student staff within a residential life or student engagement setting. Demonstrated experience supporting Living-Learning Communities, academic initiatives, or program assessment efforts. Physical Requirements Sedentary Work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/425": {
      "title": "Director, Payroll Services",
      "description": "Category: Finance, Budget, and Planning JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Director of Payroll Services oversees the daily operations of the Payroll Services Department. Responsible for payroll reporting including taxes, journal entries, disbursement of payroll-related deductions, as well as projects as they arise; works with AP, Accounting, HR and other departments to maintain financial records. The Director of Payroll Services oversees the daily operations of the Payroll Services Department. Responsible for payroll reporting, including taxes, journal entries, and disbursement of payroll-related deductions, as well as projects as they arise; works with AP, Accounting, HR, and other departments to maintain financial records. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Lead the development and administration of programs, procedures, and guidelines to help align the department with the strategic goals of the university. Participate with payroll staff in developing department goals, objectives, and systems. Oversee and review the accuracy of all payrolls, along with tax reporting and processing, including but not limited to: 941 and W-2s. Responsible for reconciling liability accounts. Complete payments to vendors. Prepare year-end financial entries and assists with any financial reporting for the payroll process. Assists IT and HR with development of reports to help with analysis of data in collaboration with IT analysts. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to maintain knowledge of all state and federal laws related to payroll issues. Ability to maintain knowledge of IRS regulations. Ability to effectively coordinate and use complex automated payroll/personnel systems. Awareness of FLSA requirements, rules and regulations. -Ability to efficiently use a personal computer and associated software (Excel, Microsoft Office) and 10-key calculator. Ability to perform complex payroll calculations accurately. Ability to communicate effectively by expressing ideas clearly and concisely. Ability to maintain confidentiality. Ability to interact in an effective and appropriate manner with diverse populations, the University community and the public. Ability to supervise personnel and complete all associated personnel actions in a timely and accurate manner. Ability to prepare and maintain accurate records and reports. Required Minimum Qualifications B.S. Degree in Accounting or a related field. Minimum of five (5) years of previous experience in payroll administration. A minimum of two (2) years of supervisory experience. Previous experience balancing and preparing W-2’s, quarterly tax reporting, and year-end processing. A background and credit check will be required of the successful applicant. Preferred: CPP and experience with Oracle Cloud-based system. Physical Requirements Sedentary Work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/427": {
      "title": "Lead Teacher (Childcare Associate)",
      "description": "Category: Auxiliary Services JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Childcare Associate reports to the Director of Little Govs University (LGU) and leads the daily learning environment for children ages 2½ to 5. The position plans and delivers developmentally appropriate instruction, supports classroom teachers, substitutes, and student workers, and serves as their first point of contact for curriculum and child behavior questions. The Childcare Associate maintains a safe, welcoming classroom; communicates with families about each child’s experience; and ensures classroom practices and records meet applicable licensing and program standards. The Childcare Associate reports to the Director of Little Govs University (LGU) and leads the daily learning environment for children ages 2½ to 5. The position plans and delivers developmentally appropriate instruction, supports classroom teachers, substitutes, and student workers, and serves as their first point of contact for curriculum and child behavior questions. The Childcare Associate maintains a safe, welcoming classroom; communicates with families about each child’s experience; and ensures classroom practices and records meet applicable licensing and program standards. Characteristics of a successful candidate: • A warm, attentive approach to children and families, with sound judgment and consistent follow-through. • Ability to guide colleagues, communicate clearly, and address classroom questions constructively. • Commitment to inclusive, developmentally appropriate early childhood practice and positive guidance. • Careful attention to children’s safety, documentation, confidentiality, and licensing requirements. • Willingness to learn, collaborate, and contribute to the continuous improvement of LGU. Primary Duties and Responsibilities : Classroom Leadership and Child Development • Provide day-to-day leadership and guidance to classroom teachers, substitutes, and APSU student workers. • Serve as the first point of contact for staff questions about curriculum, children’s behavior, and classroom concerns. • Plan and conduct a child development program that addresses each child’s physical, social, emotional, and intellectual needs. • Prepare and lead developmentally appropriate group and individual activities aligned with the Tennessee Early Learning Developmental Standards (TNELDS); post weekly lesson plans. • Provide opportunities for conversation, imaginative play, creativity, thinking, and problem-solving. • Use positive guidance to support children’s self-control and healthy relationships with others. Safety, Operations, and Compliance • Maintain constant supervision of children, arrange classroom space effectively, and ensure equipment is properly maintained. • Carry out routines promptly and hygienically in ways consistent with child development practices. • Create a welcoming classroom in which children feel comfortable and safe. • Operate the classroom in compliance with applicable licensing standards, Tennessee assessment requirements, and environmental rating scale practices. • Maintain accurate classroom records, including weekly lesson plans, family involvement documentation, observations, nap charts, and records required by the Tennessee Department of Human Services (DHS). • Use Procare daily for timekeeping, family communication, daily photographs, and name-to-face counts. Family Engagement and Center Leadership • Communicate with families daily about their children’s experiences and participate in scheduled family conferences. • Meet with the Director monthly and serve as the staff point of contact when the Director and Assistant Director are away from the center. • Participate in staff meetings, workshops, in-service training, and Student Affairs Division meetings. • Promote LGU’s philosophy and objectives, uphold the NAEYC Code of Ethical Conduct, and complete ongoing professional development required by DHS and the center. • Participate in center planning and improvement efforts. Department and Division • Maintain open communication with the Director and Assistant Director about classroom operations, children’s needs, family concerns, staffing matters, and opportunities to improve the program. • Work with center leadership to coordinate classroom activities, family engagement opportunities, and center events. • Use classroom materials and supplies responsibly and communicate resource needs to center leadership. • Collaborate with center colleagues and appropriate university partners to support children’s learning and well-being. • Prepare timely and accurate reports as requested by center leadership. • Stay informed about early childhood practices, licensing requirements, and relevant guidance; share useful information with classroom staff. • Participate in relevant professional organizations as appropriate. Required Education and Experience: • High school diploma or equivalent and a current Child Development Associate (CDA) credential, or an associate degree or higher in early childhood education, child development, or a closely related field. • At least two years of experience teaching children in an early childhood classroom or licensed child care setting. • Ability to meet all applicable Tennessee DHS child care staff eligibility, background check, and training requirements. Preferred Skills and Qualifications: Complementing the required qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree in early childhood education, child development, or a closely related field. • Experience leading a preschool classroom and coaching teachers, substitutes, or student workers. • Knowledge of the Tennessee Early Learning Developmental Standards and experience using observations to adapt learning activities. • Experience with environmental rating scales, family engagement, and child care software such as Procare. • Strong communication, organization, and judgment when addressing children’s needs and collaborating with families and colleagues. Core Competencies and Work Requirements: • Communicate effectively with children, families, colleagues, and the public; work respectfully with people from varied backgrounds. • Maintain confidential records accurately in paper and electronic systems and manage competing classroom needs. • Maintain active supervision, apply positive child guidance, and respond promptly to safety concerns. • Safely lift up to 40 pounds and work directly with children ages 2½ to 5. • Work flexible daytime hours and occasional evenings and Saturdays as needed. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/426": {
      "title": "Director, Carroll Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Director of the Carroll Entrepreneurship Center provides leadership for a university-wide, community-facing initiative designed to cultivate innovation, support new venture creation, and strengthen the Clarksville/Montgomery County regional economy. The Director will develop and lead programs that connect APSU students, faculty, alumni, entrepreneurs, investors, and community partners while positioning the University as an essential partner in the region’s entrepreneurial ecosystem. The Director reports to the Dean of the College of Business and works collaboratively with academic and administrative leaders across the University, the Center’s Advisory Board, and external community partners. The Director of the Carroll Entrepreneurship Center provides leadership for a university-wide, community-facing initiative designed to cultivate innovation, support new venture creation, and strengthen the Clarksville/Montgomery County regional economy. The Director will develop and lead programs that connect APSU students, faculty, alumni, entrepreneurs, investors, and community partners while positioning the University as an essential partner in the region’s entrepreneurial ecosystem. The Director reports to the Dean of the College of Business and works collaboratively with academic and administrative leaders across the University, the Center’s Advisory Board, and external community partners. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Lead the Center’s strategic direction and operations, developing annual programs and initiatives aligned with the Center’s mission and APSU’s institutional priorities. Build and strengthen the regional entrepreneurial ecosystem by developing relationships with entrepreneurs, business leaders, investors, economic development organizations, civic organizations, government agencies, and other community partners, with particular attention to the opportunities and needs of veteran and military-connected entrepreneurs. Develop and oversee entrepreneurship programming for APSU students and community entrepreneurs, including workshops, founder sprints, pitch competitions, mentoring, and other experiential learning opportunities. Lead the APSU Student Pitch Competition and other initiatives that identify, develop, and support promising student ventures. Support faculty innovation and commercialization by connecting faculty from across the University with resources and partners that can help translate research, creative work, and professional expertise into market- or community-ready applications. Administer the Center’s Community Microgrant Program, including developing funding priorities, managing application and review processes, monitoring awards, and assessing outcomes. Coordinate closely with the APSU Small Business Development Center (SBDC) to create an effective pipeline of support for entrepreneurs, ensuring that services complement rather than duplicate existing resources. Engage students in the Center’s work, including through Entrepreneurship Fellows, research, venture evaluation, program delivery, and other high-impact learning experiences. Convene and work with the Center’s Advisory Board, using its expertise and connections to strengthen programming, partnerships, and regional impact. Develop sustainable funding and partnership opportunities in collaboration with APSU leadership and the APSU Foundation, including corporate sponsorships, grants, government partnerships, and philanthropic support. Track, evaluate, and communicate the Center’s impact, including student participation, venture creation and growth, faculty commercialization, community engagement, strategic partnerships, funding leveraged, and regional economic impact. Represent APSU and the Carroll Entrepreneurship Center at relevant community, regional, and national entrepreneurship events and organizations. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The Director will be expected to demonstrate measurable progress in student entrepreneurship, faculty innovation and commercialization, new venture development, community engagement, strategic partnerships, funding leveraged, and regional economic impact while establishing the Carroll Entrepreneurship Center as a recognized resource for entrepreneurs throughout APSU and the Clarksville/Montgomery County community. Required Minimum Qualifications A Bachelor’s degree; advanced degree preferred. Demonstrated experience in entrepreneurship, innovation, venture development, economic development, business development, or a related field. Experience developing and managing programs, partnerships, or initiatives involving multiple stakeholders. Strong interpersonal, communication, organizational, and relationship-building skills. Demonstrated ability to work effectively across academic disciplines and with external community partners. An entrepreneurial mindset and the ability to identify opportunities, build relationships, and translate ideas into action. Physical Requirements Sedentary Work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/424": {
      "title": "Athletic Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Category: Athletic Coaching, Training and Program Management JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States We are in search of an Academic Advisor for certain sport teams as assigned. Specifically assisting in assessing student-athlete course performance, advising student athletes each semester during the pre-registration process by monitoring their class schedules for graduate requirements and special athletic needs. Also responsible to help students understand University and degree requirements and develop responsible approach to academic planning, and assisting student athletes in selecting and declaring an academic major Primary Duties and Responsibilities Serve as the academic advisor for assigned sports. Assist student-athletes in understanding University and degree requirements and develop a responsible approach to academic planning. Assist student-athletes in selecting and declaring an academic major. Assist and advise student-athletes each semester during the pre-registration process by monitoring their class schedules for graduate requirements and special athletic needs, such as travel and practice times. Monitor study hall, maintain accurate academic records, develop statistical analysis of academic success or challenges and provide data as requested regarding the academic progress of student-athletes on an on-going basis. Communicate with coaches and track the admission status, assessment and pre-registration of assigned student-athletes. Assist coaches in the recruitment process of student-athletes by sharing academic information and by meeting prospective student-athletes for campus visits. Assist student-athletes who have exhausted their eligibility in completing their degree at APSU . Assist upperclassmen in all graduation matters, e.g. career counseling, letters of recommendation, post-graduate testing and application, etc. Assist with orientation workshops for all freshman and transfer student-athletes. Refer student-athletes to other office and campus resources as needed. Oversee tutoring program and travel letter distribution for all teams. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to perform primary duties and responsibilities of the position. Ability to efficiently operate a personal computer and associated software (Outlook, Word, Excel, etc.) Banner and TeamWorks. Ability to communicate effectively and appropriately. Ability to maintain confidentiality of records and information. Ability to interact in an effective and appropriate manner with the University community and the public. Ability to maintain files accurately, in paper and in software programs. Ability to handle multiple tasks simultaneously. Ability to relate to student-athletes, coaches, administrators, faculty and parents. Ability to interpret and adhere to NCAA Rules, APSU Academic Standards and the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act of 1974. Ability to work occasional nights/weekends as needed. Ability to meet the needs of student-athletes experiencing adjustment or academic difficulties. Ability to monitor continuing eligibility and satisfactory progress of student-athletes each semester/term using APR , NCAA and University guidelines. Knowledge of University and degree requirements. Minimum Requirements Bachelor’s degree. A minimum of two years of full-time experience in athletic academic advising at the intercollegiate level. A background check will be required of the successful applicant. An official transcript and names, addresses and phone numbers of three (3) references will be required for the successful applicant. Physical Requirements Sedentary Work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/422": {
      "title": "Director, Communications",
      "description": "Category: Communications, Marketing, and Events JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Director of Communication for the College of Education provides strategic leadership and oversight of all marketing and communication initiatives for the college. This role is responsible for developing and executing the college’s comprehensive communication and marketing strategy, managing an annual marketing budget of at least $50,000, and ensuring alignment with the college’s mission, vision, and strategic priorities. The Director supervises staff, student workers, and ambassadors, while serving as the primary liaison between the college and the university’s Office of Public Relations and Marketing. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Strategic Planning & Marketing Management Develop, implement, and evaluate the College of Education annual marketing and communication plan, including managing a minimum $50,000 budget, including a digital marketing campaign with a minimum $25,000 budget. Design, coordinate, and oversee campaigns that promote student recruitment, program growth, faculty achievements, and community engagement. Leadership & Supervision Provide leadership and direction for the college’s communication efforts, ensuring alignment across all platforms and initiatives. Media & Public Relations Write, edit, and distribute press releases highlighting the college’s programs, students, faculty research, and achievements. Serve as the college liaison with the APSU Office of Public Relations and Marketing. Build and maintain relationships with media outlets to increase visibility of the college. Digital & Social Media Oversight Oversee the college’s social media presence, with content created and managed by student workers under the Director’s supervision. Ensure consistency, professionalism, and brand alignment in all digital platforms. Publications & Reports Lead the creation and publication of the College of Education Annual Report, coordinating content across departments and programs. Develop promotional and informational materials in support of advancement, recruitment, and community engagement initiatives. Other Responsibilities Serve as a member of the College of Education leadership team to align communication strategies with college-wide goals. Perform other related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strategic leadership in communication, marketing, and branding initiatives. Strong writing, editing, and storytelling skills across multiple platforms. Ability to manage budgets and evaluate ROI of communication campaigns. Experience supervising and mentoring staff, students, or interns. Proficiency in digital marketing, social media management, and analytics. Strong collaboration skills and the ability to represent the college to internal and external audiences. Required Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Communications, Public Relations, or related field. Minimum of four (4) years of progressively responsible experience in marketing, public relations, or communications. Demonstrated experience in supervising staff or student workers. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Marketing, Communications, Business Administration, or related field. Experience in higher education or nonprofit communication leadership. Demonstrated success in managing digital marketing campaigns and budgets. Physical Requirements Light Work: Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 10 pounds of force frequently, and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/406": {
      "title": "Police Officer",
      "description": "Category: Campus Safety JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Police Officer works under general supervision of a shift or operations supervisor and the Director of Public Safety/Chief of Campus Police. The Police Officer is responsible for ensuring a safe and secure campus environment; and the enforcement of University policies, state and local laws. The Police Officer works under general supervision of a shift or operations supervisor and the Director of Public Safety/Chief of Campus Police. The Police Officer is responsible for ensuring a safe and secure campus environment; and the enforcement of University policies, state and local laws. Primary Responsibilities - Crime prevention, campus patrol, radio communications, parking and traffic enforcement, criminal investigations and follow-up, and report writing. -Provide protection for University persons, property, and guests. -Maintain surveillance of all areas within department jurisdiction. -Identify and report hazards to safety and security of the campus. -Interact with other law enforcement agencies when appropriate. -Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities -Ability to recognize safety and security hazards on campus and take appropriate corrective action. -Ability to operate a vehicle. -Ability to work any shift. -Ability to pursue suspects/suspicious individuals on foot, through University buildings, grounds and make arrests as needed. -Ability to perform security and police duties on bicycle patrol. -Ability to react quickly and calmly in emergency situations. -Ability to provide protection and apply law enforcement procedures in a safe and proper manner. -Ability to ascertain facts through personal contact, observation, and examination of records. -Ability to pass annual weapon qualification to meet P.O.S.T. certification. -Ability to see, hear, and communicate effectively, especially with students and visitors to the campus. -Ability to interact in an effective and appropriate manner with diverse populations, the University community and the public Physical Requirements - Ability to pursue suspects/suspicious individuals on foot, through University buildings, grounds and make arrests as needed. - Ability to run, jump, and physically restrain an individual as needed to make arrest. Minimum Requirements - Required to be 21 years of age or older. - Must be a U.S. citizen. - Must have current P.O.S.T. certification. - High school graduate or equivalent. - Must have no criminal convictions. - Must pass a psychological examination. - Must pass a thorough background investigation conducted by the University. - Must pass a physical examination by a licensed physician at the candidate’s own expense. - Valid driver’s license. - Must have a telephone for emergency recall by department. - Essential employee will be required to report to work during emergency or disaster situations . "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/403": {
      "title": "School of Nursing - Clinical Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Austin Peay State University School of Nursing invites applications for a nine-month, clinical-track faculty position beginning July 30, 2027. We are searching for qualified applicants with multiple specialties in Nursing. Austin Peay State University is located just 40 miles north of Nashville. This program is highly competitive and was recently ranked among the top 100 nursing programs for value. BSN graduates consistently have exceptional NCLEX pass rates, well above national average. The program is proud of its facilities with state of the art classroom and simulation labs. Online teaching includes the MSN program and RN to BSN courses. The RN to BSN program is growing and expanding to meet the needs of the community. Austin Peay State University School of Nursing invites applications for a nine-month, clinical-track faculty position beginning July 30, 202 7 . We are searching for qualified applicants with multiple specialties in Nursing.. Austin Peay State University is located just 40 miles north of Nashville. This program is highly competitive and was recently ranked among the top 100 nursing programs for value. BSN graduates consistently have exceptional NCLEX pass rates, well above national average. The program is proud of its facilities with state of the art classroom and simulation labs. Online teaching includes the MSN program and RN to BSN courses. The RN to BSN program is growing and expanding to meet the needs of the community. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teach 30 hours per academic year of clinical and didactic content in the undergraduate nursing. Engage in scholarly and creative activity consistent with the School of Nursing if desired. Willingness to pursue grant funding is desirable. Teach classroom content and clinical. Be willing to teach in a variety of area s including on or off campus . Clinical teaching responsibilities include day and/or night hours; week day and/or weekends. Evidenced-based knowledge of area of discipline to be taught. Commitment to innovative and effective teaching. Assessment and grading of student work. Willingness and ability to work effectively with diverse groups of students, faculty, and staff. Commitment to university and department mission. Use of relevant technology for teaching and communication. Hold office hours every week which include participation in academic advising, and attendance in departmental and university meetings as requested or required. Maintain an active program of professional development. Provide service to department, university, local health committees and the profession. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrate teamwork and collaborative skills. Demonstrate innovation in teaching. Demonstrate knowledge of teaching assessment and evaluation. Demonstrate commitment to ongoing scholarly development. Demonstrate effective communication skills. Ability to establish and maintain effective professional relationships with students, colleagues, and supervisors. Ability to communicate clearly, effectively, and professionally through oral and written communications. Physical Requirements Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Required Minimum Qualifications MSN required Preferred: Doctorate degree in Nursing or related field. Hold an unencumbered TN RN license. Documented expertise in maternal newborn nursing. Successful experience in teaching and scholarly activities preferred Doctorate degree required for tenure and/or promotion. A background search will be required for the successful applicant. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/400": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Austin Peay State University School of Nursing invites applications for a non-tenure-track, three-year renewable, full-time clinical track nursing position beginning July 30, 2027. The position will have clinical teaching as the focus of their workload with undergraduate nursing students. The School of Nursing is housed in a state-of-the-art technology building that includes smart classrooms and state of the art simulation labs. The program offers a traditional BSN, online RN to BSN and Graduate Nursing programs. Austin Peay State University School of Nursing invites applications for a non-tenure-track, three-year renewable, full-time clinical track nursing position beginning July 30, 2027. The position will have clinical teaching as the focus of the workload with undergraduate nursing students. The School of Nursing is housed in a state-of-the-art technology building that includes smart classrooms and state-of-the-art simulation labs. The program offers a traditional BSN, online RN to BSN, and Graduate Nursing programs. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Faculty are responsible for 12-15 hours of teaching per week, which includes working closely with clinical facilities to ensure student success. Teaching in this appointment includes a variety of modalities, which may include an online or virtual environment, and other assignments to meet the needs of the college as determined by the Director of Nursing. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities · l eadership experience · commitment to innovative and effective teaching · commitment to university mission · ability to work independently and meet deadlines with little or no direction · the ability to establish and maintain effective professional relationships with students, colleagues, and supervisors · the ability to communicate clearly, effectively, and professionally through oral and written communications · ability to collaborate with clinical facilities to ensure student success · computer literacy Physical Requirements Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to life, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Work involves sitting most of the time. Walking and standing are required occasionally. Required Minimum Qualifications Faculty teaching in the baccalaureate program must have: · Baccalaureate degree in Nursing (CCNE) · G raduate nursing degree · S ignificant clinical experience; minimum 3 years of experience · recent teaching experience preferred · Candidate must be eligible for an unencumbered RN license in Tennessee Nursing specialty experience is preferred. · A background search will be required of the successful candidate. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/411": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Capital Planning and  Project Management",
      "description": "Category: Finance, Budget, and Planning JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Executive Director of Capital Planning and Project Management is responsible for leading the strategic planning, design, and execution of both capital construction initiatives and enterprise-wide business transformation projects. This position ensures the successful delivery of infrastructure and organizational initiatives that align with institutional goals, regulatory standards, and operational efficiency. This position reports to the Vice President for Finance & Administration. The Executive Director of Capital Planning and Project Management is responsible for leading the strategic planning, design, and execution of both capital construction initiatives and enterprise-wide business transformation projects. This position ensures the successful delivery of infrastructure and organizational initiatives that align with institutional goals, regulatory standards, and operational efficiency. This position reports to the Vice President for Finance & Administration. Key Responsibilities: Capital Planning, Design, and Construction Direct and manage the formulation and execution of strategic capital projects aligned with institutional priorities Supervise 3 direct reports: 2 x Architects/Project Managers and 1 x Office Assistant Manage the creation of feasibility and engineering studies Oversee architectural and engineering design processes, ensuring compliance with state laws and policies, relevant codes, and institutional standards Oversee all phases of capital construction projects from concept through closeout. Administer contracts with external contractors, architects, and engineers to ensure quality, timeliness, and budget adherence University Liaison with state agencies for approvals, inspections, and reporting coordination of university projects Establish and maintain relationships and communicate project status, progress, and issues to key stakeholders and project sponsors, both internal and external Responsible for the fulfillment and updating of the Campus Building Master Plan Enterprise Business Initiatives Lead cross-functional teams in the planning, execution, and closeout of complex, enterprise-wide initiatives. Ensure project delivery by aligning timelines, resources, and stakeholders across departments and external partners. Oversee project schedules and milestones to achieve successful outcomes within scope and budget. Budget & Compliance Develop and manage capital budgets ranging from lower-cost to multimillion-dollar initiatives. Collaborate with leadership to manage enterprise initiative budgets. Ensure compliance with state procurement laws, grant requirements, and institutional policies. Prepare reports and presentations for executive leadership and governing boards. Team Leadership & Collaboration Supervise project managers, architects, and administrative staff. Foster a culture of accountability, transparency, and continuous improvement. Serve as a liaison between APSU and external vendors, consultants, and regulatory bodies. Maintain relationships as a university representative with counterparts in other public universities and state agencies. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities: Strong knowledge of project management methodologies, including PMP certification standards. Proven ability to lead and manage large-scale projects and project teams over extended periods of time. Excellent project management skills, including scope, timeline, budget, and resource management. Effective communication and stakeholder engagement skills to collaborate with internal departments and external partners. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills to address system issues and project challenges. Ability to facilitate training plans and change management efforts to drive adoption of new systems and processes. Ability to lead cross-functional teams and foster a culture of accountability and continuous improvement. Capability to manage all phases of projects from concept through closeout, ensuring quality and compliance. Familiarity with higher education systems, workflows, and regulatory standards. Required Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Architecture, Engineering, Business, Construction Management, or related field. Military equivalent experience will be accepted in lieu of a degree. Minimum 4 years of progressive experience overseeing complex projects. Minimum 4 years of progressive supervisory experience. Preferred Qualifications Master’s Degree in Business, Project Management, Architecture, Engineering, Construction Management, Supply Chain/Logistics, or related field. Military equivalent experience will be accepted in lieu of a degree. 7 years of progressive experience leading and overseeing complex projects, including responsibility for scope, schedule, budget, and team coordination. Project Management Institute PMP® Certification or equivalent Project Management certification OR Lean Six Sigma certification OR significantly demonstrated experience in process improvement methodologies. Experience working in a higher education environment. Experience working with State Agencies and Legislative Committees Physical Requirements: Sedentary work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/364": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor (1 Year) - Educational Specialties",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Eriksson College of Education at Austin Peay State University (APSU) invites applications for a one-year visiting Assistant Professor in the Educational Specialties department, primarily in the MAEd Educational Leadership Studies program, beginning July 30, 2027. The Eriksson College of Education at Austin Peay State University (APSU) invites applications for a one-year visiting Assistant Professor in the Educational Specialties department, primarily in the MAEd Educational Leadership Studies program, beginning July 30, 2027. This practitioner-focused program is designed to prepare aspiring school leaders for principal licensure in Tennessee. Coursework is grounded in applied leadership contexts and aligned to the Tennessee Instructional Leadership Standards (TILS). Candidates with direct school and/or district leadership experience are strongly encouraged to apply. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Responsibilities include: Ability and willingness to work collaboratively with colleagues while supporting the mission of the College and University Graduate-level teaching in educational leadership, primarily in the MAEd program Academic advising and student support Service to the department, College, and University Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Possess the knowledge, talents, and skills in educational leadership to support effective teaching Ability to communicate effectively Ability to interact in an effective and appropriate manner with diverse populations in the University setting and the public Ability to problem-solve and think critically Ability to collaborate for program support and continuous improvement Experience with online course design with updates in current research and professional practices Experience with online teaching and student support Preferred expertise in one or more of the following areas: School law Instructional leadership School improvement Organizational leadership Principal preparation, educator licensure, or field-based mentorship Serving on dissertation committees Teaching educational generalist courses Physical Requirements Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift , carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Required Minimum Qualifications Candidates with the following experiences are strongly encouraged to apply: Earned doctorate (EdD or Ph.D.) from an accredited institution in Educational Leadership or a closely related field. ABD with a degree conferral by July 30, 2027 would be considered. Demonstrated P-12 school or district leadership experience (e.g., principal, assistant principal, district administrator, instructional coach) Familiarity with Tennessee educator licensure requirements and principal preparation standards Experience teaching or mentoring adult learners in applied or field-based settings. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/372": {
      "title": "Instructor - Chemistry",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Austin Peay State University invites applications for individuals seeking a full-time instructor position (three-year, renewable, nontenure contract role) for the Department of Chemistry. This position is face-to-face/in-person teaching on the Clarksville campus starting in July 30, 2027 Job Description Austin Peay State University invites applications for individuals seeking a full-time instructor position (three-year, renewable, nontenure contract role) for the Department of Chemistry. This position is face-to-face/in-person teaching on the Clarksville campus starting in July 30, 2027. This position offers an excellent opportunity to gain teaching experience in a supportive, student-centered department with a strong commitment to undergraduate education. The Department of Chemistry fosters collaboration among faculty and provides access to well-equipped teaching laboratories and shared instructional resources. Primary Duties and Responsibilities The successful candidate will teach lecture and laboratory courses in introductory and general chemistry within the American Chemical Society-accredited Department of Chemistry. The instructor may have opportunities to teach additional upper-division courses within their field of study, depending on their experience and the Department's needs. Physical Requirements Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Required Minimum Qualifications - Master's degree in Chemistry or higher. - Demonstrated success as a teacher preferred. - Demonstrated commitment to effective, inclusive teaching in introductory and general chemistry. - Preference given to candidates with experience in Inorganic or Materials Chemistry, but all specialties considered. - A background search will be required of the successful applicant. Special Instructions to Applicants Each applicant must include the names and contact information for three references, one of which must be from your most recent or current employer, with your application materials. Many people add this to the end of the CV. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/368": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Philosophy and Religion",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The APSU Department of History and Philosophy seeks a tenure-track Assistant Professor in the Philosophy and Religion Program, beginning July 30, 2027. Candidates must have a PhD and be prepared to teach courses in the History of Philosophy, especially Ancient through Modern, Epistemology, Philosophy of Religion, and World Religions. The position will be responsible for advising students in both Philosophical Studies and Religious Studies concentrations. We are searching for an experienced teacher with demonstrated ability to engage students. A record of publication is preferred. The APSU Department of History and Philosophy seeks a tenure-track Assistant Professor in the Philosophy and Religion Program, beginning July 30, 2027. Candidates must have a PhD in History, Philosophy, or related discipline and be prepared to teach courses in the History of Philosophy, especially Ancient through Modern, Epistemology, Philosophy of Religion, and World Religions. The position will be responsible for advising students in both Philosophical Studies and Religious Studies concentrations. We are searching for an experienced teacher with demonstrated ability to engage students. A record of publication is preferred. Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Unofficial Transcript Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/369": {
      "title": "Instructor - Art & Design Foundations",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Austin Peay State University Department of Art + Design invites applications for a full-time Instructor in Foundations to support the first-year experience for students studying art and design. This is a three-year, renewable position which will begin July 30, 2027. The teaching responsibilities will be on campus in Clarksville, Tennessee. The Austin Peay State University Department of Art + Design invites applications for a full-time Instructor in Foundations to support the first-year experience for students studying art and design. This is a three-year, renewable position which will begin July 30, 2027. The teaching responsibilities will be on campus in Clarksville, Tennessee. The Department of Art + Design is accredited by the National Association of Schools of Art and Design and offers BFA and BA degrees with concentrations in Studio Art, Graphic Design, Animation and Visual Effects, Art History, and Art Education. The department consists of eighteen full-time faculty, three support staff, and twelve part-time instructors who celebrate the mission of teaching and innovation in serving 250+ undergraduate majors. On-campus galleries and the growing art communities of Clarksville and Nashville provide ample opportunities for professional and student exhibitions. The Department of Art and Design is comprised of 60,000 square feet of studio, classroom, and office space spanning two buildings. Austin Peay State University is located less than an hour north of Nashville in the city of Clarksville, TN, which was named the #1 Best Place to Live in 2019 by Money Magazine. Clarksville offers accessible amenities in combination with easy access to the outdoors all within an affordable lifestyle that is 13% below the national average. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Teach a 4/4 course load that may include foundational courses in drawing, two-dimensional design, three-dimensional design, digital creative technologies, and general education Introduction to Art Teach all levels of students, who come from diverse backgrounds and experiences Implement a range of pedagogy and resources in curriculum including the application of technology in creative practice Participate in the assessment of the students, program, and department Maintain an awareness of contemporary art, design, career paths in art, relevant technological advancements, and sharing those in the classroom Coordinate the ordering of supplies for the adjunct instructors teaching foundations courses Assist in the organization and communication of Foundations Portfolio Reviews Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Proficient in the fundamentals of art and design composition, materials, and theory Comprehensive understanding of contemporary artistic practices and practitioners Depth of knowledge of Adobe Creative Cloud applications The ability to manage multiple purchase orders, institutional timelines, and policies for purchasing. Required Minimum Qualifications MFA in studio art, graphic design, animation, visual effects or another related field completed by the July 30, 2027. Preferred Qualifications Practicing professional artist, effects artist, animator, or designer Depth and breadth of knowledge in a variety of artistic disciplines Passion for teaching entry-level college students One (1) year teaching experience Required Application Documents Cover Letter- Include links to images Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Portfolio of Student Work (10-20 images) Portfolio of Recent Personal Work (10-20 images) List of three References with contact information or three letters of Recommendation "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/375": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor – Educational Leadership (EdD)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Eriksson College of Education at Austin Peay State University (APSU) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in the Department of Educational Specialties beginning July 30, 2027. The EdD program prepares scholarly practitioners consistent with the Carnegie Project on the Education Doctorate (CPED) framework, emphasizing the application of research to solve complex problems of practice. The mission of the Eriksson College of Education is to prepare educators who are ethical, engaged, and effective leaders by modeling reflective practice, connecting theory to student-centered learning, and fostering continuous improvement. The Eriksson College of Education at Austin Peay State University (APSU) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in the Department of Educational Specialties beginning July 30, 2027. The EdD program prepares scholarly practitioners consistent with the Carnegie Project on the Education Doctorate (CPED) framework, emphasizing the application of research to solve complex problems of practice. The mission of the Eriksson College of Education is to prepare educators who are ethical, engaged, and effective leaders by modeling reflective practice, connecting theory to student-centered learning, and fostering continuous improvement. Responsibilities will include teaching graduate and doctoral courses, student advising, chairing and serving on dissertation committees, scholarship, professional service, and program development. The successful candidate will possess expertise in educational leadership and/or educational research, demonstrate excellence in graduate instruction using face-to-face and online delivery formats, maintain an active scholarly agenda, and work collaboratively to support the mission of the department, college, and university. C andidates should demonstrate the ability to mentor doctoral students through dissertation design, implementation, analysis, dissemination, and publication. Candidates should possess expertise in one or more of the following areas: educational leadership, leadership in K-12 and/or higher education, literacy studies, leadership in nursing or healthcare programs, and/or socioscientific studies. Candidates will also possess e xpertise in organizational change, systems thinking, strategic leadership, and policy implementation. Successful candidates should have experience teaching and mentoring students in organizational analysis, educational research methodologies, research inquiry and evaluation, assessment and measurement, analysis of educational policy, and dissertation research. Candidates should demonstrate expertise in teaching and applying qualitative and/or quantitative research methodologies. Candidates should be committed to mentoring students throughout the dissertation process in their respective methodological areas. The successful candidate will possess expertise in educational leadership and demonstrate the ability to teach doctoral and master’s-level courses in areas including leadership theory, organizational analysis, higher education administration, educational policy, and related fields. Expertise in organizational change, systems thinking, strategic leadership, and policy implementation is especially desirable. Primary Duties and Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Teach doctoral and master’s-level courses within the Department of Educational Specialties Program (EDSP) including educational leadership, leadership theory and practice, organizational analysis, research inquiry and evaluation, educational policy, research methods, assessment, evaluation, statistics, and other relevant courses, as appropriate to expertise and program needs. Advise doctoral and master’s students. Chair dissertation committees, serve as committee members, and guide doctoral students in developing, conducting, and completing quality dissertation research. Contribute to the recruitment, retention, and mentorship of doctoral students. Develop and implement curriculum, learning objectives, and course content. Contribute to program development, curriculum revision, ongoing assessment, institutional effectiveness, and continuous program improvement. Engage in ongoing scholarly activity by maintaining an active research agenda, publishing in peer-reviewed journals, presenting at professional conferences, and contributing to the advancement of the discipline. Pursue external funding opportunities and grant development, where appropriate. Demonstrate continued professional growth through participation in professional organizations, conferences, workshops, and scholarly activities. Develop collaborative partnerships with P–12 schools, higher education institutions, and community organizations. Work collaboratively with colleagues to support departmental and university initiatives. Faculty are expected to meet university Retention, Tenure, and Promotion (RTP) expectations by maintaining excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service; contributing to departmental, college, and university governance; participating in professional and community service; and engaging collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and university offices through an active on-campus presence. Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The successful candidate should demonstrate the ability to: Teach effectively in graduate and doctoral education. Work collaboratively with faculty, students, schools, and community partners. Communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Develop curriculum and assess student learning. Demonstrate respect for various learners and learning environments. Maintain high academic expectations while providing meaningful feedback and support. Apply expertise in quantitative, qualitative, mixed-methods, action research, assessment, evaluation, measurement, and/or statistics. Support doctoral students throughout the dissertation process. Physical Requirement Ability to occasionally lift, carry, push, pull, or move objects weighing up to 10 pounds. Occasional walking and standing may be required. Required Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate (EdD or Ph.D.) from an accredited institution in Educational Leadership, Higher Education, Educational Research, Research and Evaluation, or a closely related field. ABD candidates will be considered if all degree requirements are completed by the date of hire. Demonstrated excellence or strong potential for excellence in graduate and doctoral teaching in face-to-face and online environments. Demonstrated excellence or strong potential for maintaining an active scholarly research agenda. Commitment to chairing and serving on dissertation committees. Commitment to collaborative work within the doctoral program. Commitment to professional service and community engagement. Successful completion of a background check. Preferred Qualifications Preference may be given to candidates meeting one or more of the following criteria: Demonstrated expertise as a research scholar across quantitative, qualitative, and mixed-methods research. Appropriate credentials and demonstrated ability to teach introductory and advanced qualitative methods courses. Demonstrated ability to teach introductory and advanced statistics, including multivariate analysis. Demonstrated administrative leadership experience in higher education, such as program coordination, accreditation, assessment, curriculum development, or other academic administrative responsibilities. Knowledge of assessment, evaluation, measurement, and statistics. Experience working with large datasets and innovative research designs. Evidence of conducting qualitative and quantitative data analysis. Experience mentoring doctoral students and supporting dissertation research. Record of peer-reviewed publications. Experience securing or pursuing external grant funding. Experience developing collaborative partnerships with schools, colleges, universities, or community organizations. Active scholarly research agenda including publications and presentations. Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover letter Curriculum vitae Optional Documents Unofficial transcript Letter of recommendation 1 Letter of recommendation 2 Letter of recommendation 3 Teaching Philosophy Sample course syllabi from previously taught course Sample lesson plan from previously taught course "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/407": {
      "title": "Parking Operations Assistant",
      "description": "Category: Campus Safety JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Support the daily operations of the Parking & Transportation Department through parking enforcement, parking technology, fleet management support, and equipment management. Maintain accurate operational data, assist with departmental system processes, and perform the setup, activation, maintenance, and troubleshooting of parking equipment and technology. Work collaboratively with Parking & Transportation staff to promote compliance, operational efficiency, and exceptional customer service across campus. Support the daily operations of the Parking & Transportation Department through parking enforcement, parking technology, fleet management support, and equipment management. Maintain accurate operational data, assist with departmental system processes, and perform the setup, activation, maintenance, and troubleshooting of parking equipment and technology. Work collaboratively with Parking & Transportation staff to promote compliance, operational efficiency, and exceptional customer service across campus. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Parking Enforcement and Operations Conduct walking patrols of campus parking lots and facilities. Issue parking citations and enforce University parking regulations. Monitor parking areas and report hazards, damaged equipment, and maintenance concerns. Assist with disabled vehicles and provide battery jumps when appropriate. Support daily parking operations to ensure compliance and customer service standards are met. Parking Technology and Equipment Management Perform routine inspections of parking equipment to ensure proper functionality. Assist with the setup, programming, activation, testing, maintenance, and troubleshooting of parking equipment and technology. Coordinate the installation, relocation, and removal of parking equipment for special events and operational needs. Maintain inventory of parking equipment and departmental assets. Coordinate or report equipment repairs as needed. Fleet Management Support Create and maintain vehicle maintenance schedules. Ensure regular inspections of departmental vehicles and oversee preventive maintenance requirements. Maintain vehicle inventory records and schedules for departmental vehicle use. Follow all University policies, regulations, and applicable laws regarding vehicle operations. Assist in evaluating and documenting opportunities to improve the University's fleet program. Assist in developing and maintaining vehicle routes and operational procedures. Data Management and Reporting Enter, verify, and maintain accurate records within parking management systems and departmental databases. Monitor and process permits, citations, and parking system transactions to ensure accuracy. Collect, maintain, and analyze parking utilization and enforcement data to support operational planning and reporting. Assist in identifying opportunities to improve departmental processes and operational efficiency. Customer Service and Event Support Provide exceptional customer service to students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Support parking and transportation operations for athletic events, commencement ceremonies, orientation programs, and other University events. Maintain a flexible schedule to meet departmental operational needs. Assist in developing situational procedures and operational plans for parking-related incidents or special circumstances. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to interact in an effective and appropriate manner with various populations, the University community and the public. Ability to pay attention to detail Ability to work without supervision Ability to communicate effectively and appropriately. Ability to learn and use parking software Good organization, time management and multitasking abilities. Computer skills; Demonstrate ability to learn university rules and regulations; university layout, and parking rules and regulations Physical Requirements Position will involve standing, walking, driving service vehicles, lifting, sitting, and working both indoors and outdoors. Required Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma or Equivalent ; Minimum of one year of experience in parking enforcement, a public safety field, or in a position with similar duties and responsibilities. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/365": {
      "title": "Instructor (3 Year) - Educational Specialties",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Eriksson College of Education at Austin Peay State University (APSU) invites applications for a three-year temporary instructor position in the Educational Specialties department, primarily in the MAEd Educational Leadership Studies program, beginning July 30, 2027. The Eriksson College of Education at Austin Peay State University (APSU) invites applications for a three-year temporary instructor position in the Educational Specialties department, primarily in the MAEd Educational Leadership Studies program, beginning July 30, 2027. This practitioner-focused program is designed to prepare aspiring school leaders for principal licensure in Tennessee. Coursework is grounded in applied leadership contexts and aligned to the Tennessee Instructional Leadership Standards (TILS). Candidates with direct school and/or district leadership experience are strongly encouraged to apply. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Responsibilities include: Ability and willingness to work collaboratively with colleagues while supporting the mission of the College and University Graduate-level teaching in educational leadership, primarily in the MAEd program Academic advising and student support Service to the department, College, and University Administrative tasks for program support Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Possess the knowledge, talents, and skills in educational leadership to support effective teaching Ability to communicate effectively Ability to interact in an effective and appropriate manner with diverse populations in the University setting and the public Ability to problem-solve and think critically Ability to collaborate for program support and continuous improvement Experience with online course design with updates in current research and professional practices Experience with online teaching and student support Preferred expertise in one or more of the following areas: School law Instructional leadership School improvement Organizational leadership Principal preparation, educator licensure, or field-based mentorship Physical Requirements Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift , carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Required Minimum Qualifications Demonstrated P-12 school or district leadership experience (e.g., principal, assistant principal, district administrator, instructional coach) Familiarity with Tennessee educator licensure requirements and principal preparation standards Experience teaching or mentoring adult learners in applied or field-based settings Earned doctorate (EdD or Ph.D.) from an accredited institution in Educational Leadership or a closely related field. ABD with a degree conferral by July 30, 2027 would be considered. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/367": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Musical Theatre",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Austin Peay State University Department of Theatre and Dance seeks a qualified Musical Theatre candidate to begin July 30, 2027. The full-time faculty position will be tenure-track at the level of Assistant Professor. This position is specifically seeking a candidate with a strong foundation in voice pedagogy and vocal development. The ideal candidate will be passionate about growing and preparing student voices for the rigorous demands of Musical Theatre both as a competitive professional field and as a serious performing art. Our goal is for graduates of our program to be fully equipped (vocally, technically, and artistically) to enter any industry upon graduation. Austin Peay State University Department of Theatre and Dance seeks a qualified Musical Theatre candidate to begin July 30, 2027. The full-time faculty position will be tenure-track at the level of Assistant Professor. This position is specifically seeking a candidate with a strong foundation in voice pedagogy and vocal development. The ideal candidate will be passionate about growing and preparing student voices for the rigorous demands of Musical Theatre both as a competitive professional field and as a serious performing art. Our goal is for graduates of our program to be fully equipped (vocally, technically, and artistically) to enter any industry upon graduation. The Theatre and Dance program at Austin Peay State University offers a BFA with concentrations in Acting, Design, Musical Theatre, and Stage Management, and a BA with concentrations in Theatre and Dance. Minors in Theatre and Dance are popular choices for many students. An intimate proscenium theatre seating just under 200 currently houses 4-5 productions each academic year, with a Laboratory Theatre space available for additional productions, student performances, and events. Theatre and Dance are integral parts of the Center of Excellence for the Creative Arts (www.apsu.edu/creativearts). A long established, state-funded initiative, APSU’s Center of Excellence for the Creative Arts, is designed to enhance the cultural environment of the university, community, and region through a diverse range of imaginative arts experiences. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be expected to: - Teach Theatre/Musical Theatre related courses which includes Private Voice Lessons, Musical Theatre History, Musical Theatre Workshop, Voice for the Actor, Diction, Musical Theory, and may include Dance for Musical Theatre, Introduction to Theatre or other related courses as assigned based on Department needs/candidate expertise; - Serve as Musical Director or Director for Musicals during the production season - Demonstrate a willingness and an ability to work effectively with colleagues to support the mission of the institution and the department; - Advise and mentor students effectively and efficiently throughout their time in the program and help majors persist toward graduation; and - Serve effectively on Departmental and University committees and other appropriate functions that assist in University governance; and - Show a commitment to continued recruiting efforts as the program continues to grow. Physical Requirements - Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Required Minimal Qualifications The ideal candidate will meet the following: - A terminal degree (MFA or PhD) in Theatre, Musical Theatre, or a related discipline; or a terminal master's degree in a related field combined with significant professional experience in Musical Theatre at a level commensurate with terminal degree expectations. - A minimum of two (2) years teaching experience in higher education is preferred but not mandatory. - Evidence of potential ability in academic assignment and/or scholarly and creative achievement, and/or professional contributions and activities. - Evidence of good character, mature attitude, and professional integrity. - Evidence of a respect for and an ability to work with a diverse student body - A background check will be required of the successful candidate. Special Instructions to Applicants - Each applicant must include the names and contact information for three references with your application materials. Many people add this to the end of the CV. - If you would like to additionally attach Letters of Recommendation to your online application, letters must be dated one year or less from the date of your application. Letters of recommendation may be sent by email to “facultyapplications@apsu.edu” or hard copy to “Austin Peay State University, Human Resources Dept., PO Box 4507, Clarksville, TN 37044” with your name and desired position clearly indicated after your online application is completed. - If granted an interview, unofficial transcripts will be required of applicants and official transcripts will be required of the selected candidate before the candidate will be offered a position. It is highly recommended that you attach unofficial transcripts in PDF format to your online application. - You will not be able to attach your letters of recommendation, unofficial transcripts or any other supplemental document(s) nor modify your application after it has been submitted. Applicant review will continue until the position is filled. Required Documents 1. Cover Letter 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents 1. Unofficial Transcript 2. Letter of Recommendation 1 3. Letter of Recommendation 2 4. Letter of Recommendation 3 "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/366": {
      "title": "Instructor - Dance",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Austin Peay State University Department of Theatre and Dance is seeking a three-year full-time instructor for the position of Dance to begin July 31, 2027. This position is specifically seeking a candidate with a strong foundation in Commercial and Musical Theatre dance forms, including but not limited to jazz, hip-hop, tap, contemporary, and diasporic dance traditions. The ideal candidate will be passionate about training versatile, industry-ready performers who are proficient across all aspects of the performance field. Additionally, the ideal candidate will also contribute to the Acting students, teaching performance-based coursework as needed, reflecting the department's commitment to developing well-rounded performers ready for the demands of the modern industry. The Austin Peay State University Department of Theatre and Dance is seeking a three-year full-time instructor for the position of Dance to begin August 1st, 2027. This position is specifically seeking a candidate with a strong foundation in Commercial and Musical Theatre dance forms, including but not limited to jazz, hip-hop, tap, contemporary, and diasporic dance traditions. The ideal candidate will be passionate about training versatile, industry-ready performers who are proficient across all aspects of the performance field. Additionally, the ideal candidate will also contribute to the Acting students, teaching performance-based coursework as needed, reflecting the department's commitment to developing well-rounded performers ready for the demands of the modern industry. The Theatre and Dance program at Austin Peay State University offers a BFA with concentrations in Acting, Design, Musical Theatre, and Stage Management, and a BA with concentrations in Theatre and Dance. Minors in Theatre and Dance are popular choices for many students. An intimate proscenium theatre seating just under 200 currently houses 4-5 productions each academic year, with a Laboratory Theatre space available for additional productions, student performances, and events. Theatre and Dance are integral parts of the Center of Excellence for the Creative Arts (www.apsu.edu/creativearts). A long established, state-funded initiative, APSU’s Center of Excellence for the Creative Arts, is designed to enhance the cultural environment of the university, community, and region through a diverse range of imaginative arts experiences. Primary Duties and Responsibilities - Teach Dance technique in modern, jazz, tap or diasporic movement, commercial dance forms, musical theatre and related areas such as Introduction to Dance, Dance History, Dance Fundamentals and choreograph for main stage productions where needed; - Support MT and Acting BFA programs by teaching acting and/or performance courses as needed and qualified - Demonstrate a willingness and an ability to work effectively with colleagues to support the mission of the institution and the department; - Advise and mentor students effectively and efficiently throughout their time in the program and help majors persist toward graduation; - Serve effectively on departmental and University committees and other appropriate functions that assist in University governance; - Show a commitment to continued recruiting efforts as the program continues to grow. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities - Demonstrate a willingness and an ability to work effectively with colleagues to support the mission of the institution and the department; - Advise and mentor students effectively and efficiently throughout their time in the program and help majors persist toward graduation; - Serve effectively on departmental and University committees and other appropriate functions that assist in University governance; - Show a commitment to continued recruiting efforts as the program continues to grow. Physical Requirements Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Required Minimum Qualifications - A terminal degree (MFA or PhD) in Dance, Musical Theatre, or a related discipline; or a master's degree in a related field combined with significant professional experience in Dance and performance at a level commensurate with terminal degree expectations. - Evidence of potential ability in academic assignment and/or scholarly and creative achievement, and/or professional contributions and activities; - Evidence of good character, mature attitude, and professional integrity; - Evidence of a respect for and an ability to work with a diverse student body; - A background search will be required of the successful applicant. Additional Preferred Qualifications: - At least two years teaching experience in higher education preferred; - Candidates who can contribute to our curriculum in one or more of the following specialty areas: Choreography and Dance for Musical Theatre, Commercial dance, Hip-hop, diasporic dance Special Instructions to Applicants: - Each applicant must include the names and contact information for three references, one of which must be from your most recent or current employer, with your application materials. Many people add this to the end of the CV. - Two letters of recommendation must be included; - A Teaching Philosophy must be included; - If you would like to additionally attach Letters of Recommendation to your online application, letters must be dated one year or less from the date of your application. Letters of recommendation may be sent by email to “facultyapplications@apsu.edu” or hard copy to “Austin Peay State University, Human Resources Dept., PO Box 4507, Clarksville, TN 37044” with your name and desired position clearly indicated after your online application is completed. - If granted an interview, unofficial transcripts will be required of applicants and official transcripts will be required of the selected candidate before the candidate will be offered a position. It is highly recommended that you attach unofficial transcripts in PDF format to your online application. - You will not be able to attach your letters of recommendation, unofficial transcripts or any other supplemental document(s) nor modify your application after it has been submitted. Applicant review will continue until the position is filled. Required Documents 1. Cover Letter 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. Teaching Philosophy 4. Letter of Recommendation 1 5. Letter of Recommendation 2 Optional Documents 1. Unofficial Transcript 2. Letter of Recommendation 3 "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/373": {
      "title": "Instructor of Music Therapy",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Department of Music at Austin Peay State University invites applications for a nine-month Instructor of Music Therapy. This non-tenure-track appointment is a three-year term starting July 30, 2027. The Department of Music at Austin Peay State University invites applications for a nine-month Instructor of Music Therapy. This non-tenure-track appointment is a three-year term starting July 30, 2027. The Department of Music at Austin Peay State University, an accredited member of the National Association of Schools of Music, enjoys a vital presence on campus, in the Clarksville community, and in the region. The Department boasts a nationally recognized and acoustically superior concert hall, along with outstanding performance, practice, rehearsal, and studio spaces. The Department of Music is an integral member of the Center of Excellence for the Creative Arts (CECA https://apsu.edu/ceca/). A long-established state-funded initiative, CECA is designed to enhance the cultural environment of the university, community, and region through a diverse range of imaginative arts experiences. The following degrees are offered: Bachelor of Music with concentrations in Performance, Music Education, Composition, and Music Therapy; Bachelor of Arts and Bachelor of Science in Music; Master of Music with concentrations in Music Education, Performance, Collaborative Piano, Instrumental Conducting, and Choral Conducting. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teach undergraduate classes in the music therapy curriculum. Engage in professional, creative, and scholarly activities. Work with other departments across campus, and with area musicians and music therapists. Actively participate in professional organizations allied to music therapy and individual research interests. Participate in recruiting activities alone and in group settings. Serve as the clinical education coordinator, ensuring all students complete necessary clearances, foster relationships with community partners, and build relationships for future collaborations Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Organization Attention to detail Ability to work independently Strong collaborative and interpersonal skills, and a demonstrated commitment to a collegial environment Excellence as a teacher of undergraduate students Clinical musicianship competencies on guitar, piano, voice, and percussion Physical Requirements Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Required Minimum Qualifications - Master’s degree in music therapy or related discipline - Board-Certified Music Therapist (MT-BC) with at least two years of clinical experience - A commitment to the recruiting efforts of the department, college, and university. - Potential for a substantial creative/research/professional agenda. - Demonstrated aptitude for classroom teaching and personal concern for students and their achievement. Preferred: - Facility with and understanding of current technologies as they pertain to teaching and supervising music therapy students. - Documented experience in leading and supervising student clinical placements. - Demonstrated success teaching students of wide-ranging and non-traditional backgrounds at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Special Instructions to Applicants: Each applicant must include a cover letter, CV, teaching philosophy, a list of three professional references, and unofficial transcripts. Official transcripts are required upon hire. You will not be able to attach your letters of recommendation, unofficial transcripts or any other supplemental document(s) nor modify your application after it has been submitted. Review of materials will begin on November 4 and will continue until the position is filled. A background check will be required by the successful applicant. Please refer all questions to facultyapplications@apsu.edu Application Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter CV Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts List of three professional references Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Optional digital portfolio highlighting conference presentations, teaching demonstrations, and other related materials. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/374": {
      "title": "Instructor - Saxophone",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Department of Music at Austin Peay State University invites applications for a full-time, nine-month Instructor of Applied Saxophone. This non-tenure-track appointment is a three-year term beginning July 30, 2027. The Department of Music at Austin Peay State University invites applications for a full-time, nine-month Instructor of Applied Saxophone. This non-tenure-track appointment is a three-year term beginning July 30, 2027. The Department of Music at Austin Peay State University, an accredited member of the National Association of Schools of Music, enjoys a vital presence on campus, in the Clarksville community, and in the region. The Department boasts a nationally recognized and acoustically superior concert hall, along with outstanding performance, practice, rehearsal, and studio spaces. The Department of Music is an integral member of the Center of Excellence for the Creative Arts (CECA https://apsu.edu/ceca/ ). A long-established state-funded initiative, CECA is designed to enhance the cultural environment of the university, community, and region through a diverse range of imaginative arts experiences. The following degrees are offered: Bachelor of Music with concentrations in Performance, Music Education, Composition, and Music Therapy; Bachelor of Arts and Bachelor of Science in Music; Master of Music with concentrations in Music Education, Performance, Collaborative Piano, Instrumental Conducting, and Choral Conducting. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate applied saxophone and directing the saxophone ensemble. Additional teaching assignments will be determined based on departmental needs and the successful candidate's specific areas of expertise. Engage in professional, creative, and scholarly activities. Advise undergraduate and graduate students. Work with other departments across campus, and with area musicians and music educators. Actively participate in professional organizations allied to saxophone and individual research interests.] Participate in recruiting activities alone and in group settings. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Organization Attention to detail Ability to work independently Strong collaborative and interpersonal skills, and a demonstrated commitment to a collegial environment Excellence as a teacher of undergraduate and graduate students Physical Requirements Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Required Minimum Qualifications - Master’s degree in saxophone performance or related fields. - A commitment to the recruiting efforts of the department, college, and university. - Potential for a substantial creative/research/performance agenda. - Demonstrated aptitude for classroom teaching and personal concern for students and their achievement. Preferred : - Doctoral degree in saxophone performance. - Facility with and understanding of current technologies as they pertain to teaching saxophone. - Documented experience in leading student creative activities. - Demonstrated success teaching students of wide-ranging and non-traditional backgrounds at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Special Instructions to Applicants: Each applicant must include a cover letter, CV, teaching philosophy, a list of three professional references, and unofficial transcripts. Official transcripts are required upon hire. You will not be able to attach your letters of recommendation, unofficial transcripts or any other supplemental document(s) nor modify your application after it has been submitted. Review of materials will begin on November 4 and will continue until the position is filled. A background check will be required by the successful applicant. Please refer all questions to facultyapplications@apsu.edu Application Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter CV Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts List of three professional references Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Optional digital portfolio highlighting conference presentations, teaching demonstrations, and other related materials. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/376": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor – Educational Research (EdD)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Eriksson College of Education at Austin Peay State University (APSU) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in the Department of Educational Specialties beginning July 30, 2027. The EdD program prepares scholarly practitioners consistent with the Carnegie Project on the Education Doctorate (CPED) framework, emphasizing the application of research to solve complex problems of practice. The mission of the Eriksson College of Education is to prepare educators who are ethical, engaged, and effective leaders by modeling reflective practice, connecting theory to student-centered learning, and fostering continuous improvement. The Eriksson College of Education at Austin Peay State University (APSU) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in the Department of Educational Specialties beginning July 30, 2027. The EdD program prepares scholarly practitioners consistent with the Carnegie Project on the Education Doctorate (CPED) framework, emphasizing the application of research to solve complex problems of practice. The mission of the Eriksson College of Education is to prepare educators who are ethical, engaged, and effective leaders by modeling reflective practice, connecting theory to student-centered learning, and fostering continuous improvement. Responsibilities will include teaching graduate and doctoral courses, student advising, chairing and serving on dissertation committees, scholarship, professional service, and program development. The successful candidate will possess expertise in educational leadership and/or educational research, demonstrate excellence in graduate instruction using face-to-face and online delivery formats, maintain an active scholarly agenda, and work collaboratively to support the mission of the department, college, and university. C andidates should demonstrate the ability to mentor doctoral students through dissertation design, implementation, analysis, dissemination, and publication. Candidates should possess expertise in one or more of the following areas: educational leadership, leadership in K-12 and/or higher education, literacy studies, leadership in nursing or healthcare programs, and/or socioscientific studies. Candidates will also possess e xpertise in organizational change, systems thinking, strategic leadership, and policy implementation. Successful candidates should have experience teaching and mentoring students in organizational analysis, educational research methodologies, research inquiry and evaluation, assessment and measurement, analysis of educational policy, and dissertation research. Candidates should demonstrate expertise in teaching and applying qualitative and/or quantitative research methodologies. Candidates should be committed to mentoring students throughout the dissertation process in their respective methodological areas. The successful candidate will possess expertise in educational research and demonstrate the ability to teach doctoral and master’s-level courses in areas including research methods, quantitative and qualitative research design, statistics, assessment, program evaluation, and related fields. Primary Duties and Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Teach doctoral and master’s-level courses within the Department of Educational Specialties Program (EDSP) including educational leadership, leadership theory and practice, organizational analysis, research inquiry and evaluation, educational policy, research methods, assessment, evaluation, statistics, and other relevant courses, as appropriate to expertise and program needs. Advise doctoral and master’s students. Chair dissertation committees, serve as committee members, and guide doctoral students in developing, conducting, and completing quality dissertation research. Contribute to the recruitment, retention, and mentorship of doctoral students. Develop and implement curriculum, learning objectives, and course content. Contribute to program development, curriculum revision, ongoing assessment, institutional effectiveness, and continuous program improvement. Engage in ongoing scholarly activity by maintaining an active research agenda, publishing in peer-reviewed journals, presenting at professional conferences, and contributing to the advancement of the discipline. Pursue external funding opportunities and grant development, where appropriate. Demonstrate continued professional growth through participation in professional organizations, conferences, workshops, and scholarly activities. Develop collaborative partnerships with P–12 schools, higher education institutions, and community organizations. Work collaboratively with colleagues to support departmental and university initiatives. Faculty are expected to meet university Retention, Tenure, and Promotion (RTP) expectations by maintaining excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service; contributing to departmental, college, and university governance; participating in professional and community service; and engaging collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and university offices through an active on-campus presence. Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The successful candidate should demonstrate the ability to: Teach effectively in graduate and doctoral education. Work collaboratively with faculty, students, schools, and community partners. Communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Develop curriculum and assess student learning. Demonstrate respect for various learners and learning environments. Maintain high academic expectations while providing meaningful feedback and support. Apply expertise in quantitative, qualitative, mixed-methods, action research, assessment, evaluation, measurement, and/or statistics. Support doctoral students throughout the dissertation process. Physical Requirement Ability to occasionally lift, carry, push, pull, or move objects weighing up to 10 pounds. Occasional walking and standing may be required. Required Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate (EdD or Ph.D.) from an accredited institution in Educational Leadership, Higher Education, Educational Research, Research and Evaluation, or a closely related field. ABD candidates will be considered if all degree requirements are completed by the date of hire. Demonstrated excellence or strong potential for excellence in graduate and doctoral teaching in face-to-face and online environments. Demonstrated excellence or strong potential for maintaining an active scholarly research agenda. Commitment to chairing and serving on dissertation committees. Commitment to collaborative work within the doctoral program. Commitment to professional service and community engagement. Successful completion of a background check. Preferred Qualifications Preference may be given to candidates meeting one or more of the following criteria: Demonstrated expertise as a research scholar across quantitative, qualitative, and mixed-methods research. Appropriate credentials and demonstrated ability to teach introductory and advanced qualitative methods courses. Demonstrated ability to teach introductory and advanced statistics, including multivariate analysis. Demonstrated administrative leadership experience in higher education, such as program coordination, accreditation, assessment, curriculum development, or other academic administrative responsibilities. Knowledge of assessment, evaluation, measurement, and statistics. Experience working with large datasets and innovative research designs. Evidence of conducting qualitative and quantitative data analysis. Experience mentoring doctoral students and supporting dissertation research. Record of peer-reviewed publications. Experience securing or pursuing external grant funding. Experience developing collaborative partnerships with schools, colleges, universities, or community organizations. Active scholarly research agenda including publications and presentations. Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover letter Curriculum vitae Optional Documents Unofficial transcript Letter of recommendation 1 Letter of recommendation 2 Letter of recommendation 3 Teaching Philosophy Sample course syllabi from previously taught course Sample lesson plan from previously taught course "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/379": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Psychological Science, Experimental",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Nominations and applications are invited for the position of Assistant Professor, Psychological Science, area of specialization is open. This is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track position to begin July 30, 2027. Nominations and applications are invited for the position of Assistant Professor, Psychological Science, area of specialization is open . This is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track position to begin July 30, 2027. The Department of Psychological Science and Counseling is a diverse, dynamic, and collegial environment that is home to a large undergraduate program in psychological science, a Master of Science program in Industrial and Organizational Psychology (MSIO), a Master of Science program in Counseling, and a PsyD program specializing in working with military families . For more information about the department, visit: http://www.apsu.edu/psychology/index.php . The department is housed within the College of Behavioral and Health Sciences which affords rich opportunities for interdisciplinary collaborations. Some examples of recent and ongoing college collaborations include a grant-funded research and intervention project aimed at supporting student veteran transitions to college, a grant-funded project focused on student mental health and wellness, a juvenile justice mentorship project, and a working group focusing on trauma-informed pedagogy. Austin Peay State University is located in Clarksville, TN, which Money Magazine rated number 1 in its 2019 Best Places to Live rankings: https://clarksvillenow.com/local/clarksville-named-best-place-to-live-by-money-magazine/ . Clarksville is a vibrant, diverse community with a low cost of living, and easy interstate access to nearby Nashville. Clarksville is centrally located in the region, with Memphis, Louisville, Atlanta, St. Louis, Chicago, Cincinnati, Indianapolis, New Orleans, and many other major cities a day’s drive away. For additional information about APSU including our mission and vision please visit: https://www.apsu.edu/about-apsu/index.php Major Responsibilities Teaching responsibilities in our recently revamped curriculum will include a range of undergraduate courses in the Bachelor of Science program, including PSYC 1030 – Introduction to Psychology and courses in the selected candidate’s specialty area. Preference will be given to candidate who can contribute to one or more of the following areas: research methodology courses, physiological psychology, brain and behavior/neurocognition, sensation and perception, cognitive psychology, and/or learning and motivation. Follow the link for a curriculum overview and a list of departmental undergraduate courses . The departmental teaching load is 12 hours each semester, which can include credit for leading research teams comprised of undergraduate researchers. Summer teaching opportunities are available. Research activity is required for this position and scholarship activities involving undergraduates will be encouraged. The department of Psychological Science currently has a variety of laboratory spaces and a collaborative developmental and play observation/lab space. In addition, the university has funding opportunities to help support research and teaching equipment expenses. Candidates who demonstrate a strong interest in undergraduate education and involving undergraduates in research, in contributing to general education teaching and advising, and in departmental service are preferred. Applicant review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. More information about the department and its programs can be found on our website: https://www.apsu.edu/psychology/ . Required Qualifications A Ph.D. in Psychology is required, with the area of specialization open. ABD will be considered if the Ph.D. will be completed by July 30, 2027. Screening of applications will continue until position is filled. Applicants should submit the following: 1. Letter of application addressing interest in the position, qualifications, and a statement of research interests 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Three Letters of Recommendation and/or names and contact information of 3 professional references (can be listed on CV) 4. Teaching Philosophy and Experience Optional: 1. Transcript "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/380": {
      "title": "Director, Master of Athletic Training Program",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States This is a tenure-track position available at the Associate or Full Professor rank (faculty/director role) beginning July 1, 2027. This is a tenure-track position available at the Associate or Full Professor rank (faculty/director role) beginning July 1, 2027. Summary Austin Peay State University's Department of Health and Human Performance seeks a dynamic leader to serve as the founding Director of the Master of Athletic Training program. The successful candidate will lead all efforts creating the new Master of Athletic Training (MAT) Program, leading to successful CAATE accreditation, with the inaugural cohort launching in Summer 2027. The successful candidate will be brought in at the Associate or Full Professor level, depending on experience and qualifications. Job Description The Department of Health and Human Performance seeks qualified applicants who meet the criteria at the Associate or Full Professor level who possess a terminal degree ( Ph.D., DAT, DSc, ScD, or EdD) in athletic training or related field. The successful candidate is also expected to be a BOC-certified athletic trainer who is eligible for licensure in the State of Tennessee. The successful candidate is expected to lead and maintain the program through the CAATE accreditation, teach classes, conduct scholarship, advise/mentor students, and provide service to the University, their profession, and the community. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Lead the MAT program through the initial CAATE accreditation and all subsequent annual reviews, re-accreditations, and other CAATE requirements. All administrative duties as required by Austin Peay to achieve program outcomes. Recruit and retain additional program faculty. Teach courses within the Kinesiology and Health and Human Performance undergraduate programs and the Master of Athletic Training graduate program. Conduct research within his/her discipline. Provide service to the Department, College, and University Required Qualifications Hold a Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree, including but not limited to EdD, DAT, DSc, ScD from an accredited institution of higher education in athletic training or a related field. Hold current national BOC certification as an Athletic Trainer and be in good standing with the Board of Certification, Inc. Be eligible for and maintain Tennessee State licensure. Demonstrated experience teaching within a CAATE-accredited athletic training program. Demonstrated experience with the CAATE accreditation processes. Have at least five years of clinical experience in athletic training. Demonstrated scholarship in athletic training (or related field). Have at least 5+ years of teaching experience in a full-time academic appointment. About the Department of Health & Human Performance The Department of Health and Human Performance (HHP) serves approximately 440 majors in two undergraduate programs: a B.S. in Kinesiology with two concentrations and a B.S. in Health and Human Performance with five concentrations. In addition, HHP has approximately 130 graduate students across four programs: Master of Healthcare Administration, Master of Science in Health and Human Performance, Master of Public Health, and Master of Speech-Language Pathology. The department houses state-of-the-art instructional and laboratory spaces in a brand new 115,000 ft 2 Health Professions Building that opened in August 2025. About Austin Peay State University Austin Peay State University (APSU), located in Clarksville, Tennessee, is a leading institution of higher education in the Southeast. The university offers over 50 graduate and 125 undergraduate degree paths, including the country’s first registered apprenticeship for teaching , a fast-growing Master of Business Administration (MBA) program, and the state’s only accredited Doctor of Psychology (PsyD) in counseling psychology program. Named after Clarksville native and former Tennessee Gov. Austin Peay, the university’s Clarksville campus spans 195 acres downtown and is home to the state-of-the-art Health Professions Building. APSU also operates a campus at Fort Campbell, Kentucky and is Tennessee’s leading higher education provider for military-affiliated students, who represent approximately 32% of the student body. For more information, visit www.apsu.edu . Starting Date : July 1, 2027 "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/370": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Art & Design - Ceramics",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Austin Peay State University Department of Art + Design invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of Art in Ceramics to lead the ceramics area at APSU. The teaching responsibilities will be on campus in Clarksville, Tennessee and will begin July 30, 2027. The Austin Peay State University Department of Art + Design invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of Art in Ceramics to lead the ceramics area at APSU. The teaching responsibilities will be on campus in Clarksville, Tennessee and will begin July 30, 2027. The current curriculum in ceramics includes a three-course sequence covering a wide range of materials, processes, techniques, and concepts including wheel-throwing, hand-building, clay and glaze mixing, and electric and gas kiln firing. The curriculum also includes stand-alone courses in ceramic sculpture and ceramic slip casting. This position offers opportunities for the successful candidate to re-imagine the focus and trajectory of the program. Candidates are also encouraged to demonstrate their experience working with innovative strategies and new technologies. Other teaching responsibilities may include courses in Foundations. There are opportunities for the development of a special topics, study away, and study abroad courses. The Department of Art + Design is accredited by the National Association of Schools of Art and Design and offers BFA and BA degrees with concentrations in Studio Art, Graphic Design, Animation and Visual Effects, Art History, and Art Education. The department consists of eighteen full-time faculty, three support staff, and twelve part-time instructors who celebrate the mission of teaching and innovation in serving 250+ undergraduate majors. On-campus galleries and the growing art communities of Clarksville and Nashville provide ample opportunities for professional and student exhibitions. The Department of Art and Design is comprised of 60,000 square feet of studio, classroom, and office space spanning two buildings. Austin Peay State University is located less than an hour north of Nashville in the city of Clarksville, TN, which was named the #1 Best Place to Live in 2019 by Money Magazine. Clarksville offers accessible amenities in combination with easy access to the outdoors all within an affordable lifestyle that is 13% below the national average. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Teach a 3/3 course load to include the ceramic studio area and foundations level courses Teach all levels of students, who come from diverse backgrounds and experiences Participate in the development of curriculum and the assessment of the students, program, and department through portfolio and capstone reviews. Maintain an awareness of contemporary art, design, career paths in art, relevant technological advancements, and sharing those in the classroom Collaborate with fellow faculty within and across departments and participate in APSU’s shared governance; partner with staff to identify and accomplish shared goals Maintain and oversee the APSU ceramics facility and student workers alongside the studio technician Advise and mentor students in their course of studies and individual research Engage in ongoing creative research and professional activities in ceramics Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The successful candidate should have experience in both traditional and innovative ceramics processes The successful candidate should have experience with the management of a ceramics studio; health and safety standards, kiln operation and maintenance, clay mixing and reclamation, and glaze mixing Comprehensive understanding of contemporary artistic practices and practitioners Required Minimum Qualifications MFA in Ceramics or related program completed by July 30, 2027. Preferred Qualifications Practicing, professional artist with a dynamic exhibition history Two (2) years of post-secondary teaching experience Physical Requirements Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or frequently to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects Required Application Documents Cover Letter- Include links to images Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy A Portfolio of Student Works (20 images) with annotated written project descriptions- You may provide link A Portfolio of Recent Personal Work (20 images)- You may provide link List of three References with contact information or three letters of Recommendation "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/377": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Counselor Education",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Applications are invited for the position of Assistant Professor of Counselor Education. This is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track position to begin July 30, 2027. Applications are invited for the position of Assistant Professor of Counselor Education . This is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track position to begin July 30, 2027. The successful candidate will teach graduate-level counseling classes, supervise counseling students, participate in service activities, and engage in research. Teaching responsibilities will include graduate courses in the M.S. in Counseling program. Specific courses may include Addiction Counseling; Counseling Techniques; Diagnosis and Psychopathology; Ethical, Legal, and Professional Issues in Counseling; Group Counseling; Psychological Assessment & Appraisal; Lifespan Development; Counseling Diverse Populations; Couples & Family Counseling; Crisis & Trauma Counseling; Counseling Theories; and other courses in areas of expertise. Summer teaching opportunities are available. Research activity is required for this position and scholarship activities involving students will be encouraged. The Department of Psychological Science currently has generous lab space, a counseling lab with suites for private sessions, and a recently opened mental health clinic. In addition, the university has funding opportunities to help support research and teaching equipment expenses. More information about the M.S. in Counseling program can be found on our program website: https://www.apsu.edu/mscounseling/ Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teach graduate courses in the M.S. in Counseling program Advise graduate students Provide supervision for graduate students Serve on program, department, and university committees Engage in research and support student-involved scholarship activities Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrate commitment to excellence in graduate-level teaching, clinical supervision, and student mentorship. Ability to effectively advise and support graduate counseling students throughout their academic and professional development. Capacity to contribute to an active research agenda, with an interest in engaging students in collaborative scholarly activities. Knowledge of and experience with CACREP-accredited counseling programs and the standards that guide counselor preparation. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work collaboratively and collegially with faculty, staff, and community partners. Commitment to fostering respectful learning environments and meeting the diverse needs of students. Willingness to teach in various modalities (e.g., in-person, online, hybrid) and at times that accommodate program needs. Demonstrated ability to contribute to program development and serve on department, college, and university committees. Knowledge and proficiency in the ethical and legal standards of the counseling profession and counselor education. Required Qualifications A Doctorate in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP-accredited program is required. ABD will be considered if the doctorate will be completed by July 30, 2027. Additional Qualifications Licensed or license-eligible as a professional counselor (LPC) in Tennessee. Experience with advising, practicum, internship & clinical supervision. Background or expertise in clinical mental health counseling. Screening of applications will continue until position is filled. Applicants should submit the following: Letter of application addressing interest in the position and qualifications Curriculum vitae Three Letters of Recommendation and/or Names and contact information of 3 professional references (can be listed on CV) Optional: Transcript Statement on Commitment to Student Success and Access "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/382": {
      "title": "Instructor of Business Communication",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Austin Peay State University’s AACSB accredited College of Business, invites applicants for an Instructor of Business Communication with teaching interests in business communication to begin July 30, 2027. This is a three-year, renewable, nontenure, contract role to teach eight three-hour courses per year: four courses in Fall; four courses in Spring. This role is eligible for the benefits provided to faculty, administrative staff, and professional staff. Austin Peay State University’s AACSB accredited College of Business, invites applicants for an Instructor of Business Communication with teaching interests in business communication to begin July 30, 2027. This is a three-year, renewable, nontenure, contract role to teach eight three-hour courses per year: four courses in Fall; four courses in Spring. This role is eligible for the benefits provided to faculty, administrative staff, and professional staff. Austin Peay State University is a comprehensive university committed to raising the educational attainment of the citizenry, developing programs and services that address regional needs, and providing collaborative opportunities that connect university expertise with private and public resources. Collectively, these endeavors contribute significantly to the intellectual, economic, social, physical, and cultural development of the region. APSU prepares students to be engaged and productive citizens, while recognizing that society and the marketplace require global awareness and continuous learning. APSU’s vision is to create a collaborative, integrative learning community, instilling in students’ habits of critical inquiry as they gain knowledge, skills and values for life and work in a global society. Austin Peay’s five core values, which set the tone for how the University works, are quality, innovation, collaboration, community and globalization. For more information about Austin Peay State University visit: https://www.apsu.edu/ Primary Duties and Responsibilities This position requires active teaching related to the discipline. Essential Functions •Possess the knowledge, talents, and skills in business communication or a closely related discipline and in multiple teaching methodologies, including hybrid, flipped, and blended courses. •Demonstrate respect for the diverse learning needs of students. •Demonstrate the ability to develop and implement curriculum objectives and content for business communication courses taught. •Demand and maintain high standards and expectations for all students. Physical Requirements Sedentary- Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects. Required Minimum Qualifications • Candidates must be qualified as Scholarly Academic (SA) or as an Instructional Practitioner (IP) per AACSB standards. To meet these standards, a candidate must have: recently earned a doctorate in communication, or earned a doctorate in communication and have recent publications related to communication (SA) or earned a Master’s degree in Communication or MBA with Business school teaching experience, and professional experience that is current, substantial in terms of duration and level of responsibility (over five years), and clearly linked to the field of Business Communication. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to the requirements of AACSB accreditation. Teaching Philosophy Statement A background search will be required of the successful candidate. Special Instructions to Applicants When submitting your CV for review, please identify each publication ranking on the Australian Business Deans Council (ABDC) list. The ranking should be either an A*, A, B, or C. If the journal is not on the ABDC list, please note this. All publications will be considered, but preference will be given to publications listed on the ABDC list. In addition, please include any significant consulting projects. If you have not completed your degree, please submit a letter from your committee chair with an anticipated completion date. The individual selected for this role must maintain qualifications to teach in the field through practice work such as consulting and/or publication of discipline-related academic research. If granted an interview, applicants will be required to provide unofficial transcripts, and the selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts before a position is offered. Applicant review will continue until the position is filled. Please refer all questions to facultyapplications@apsu.edu "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/394": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Engineering Technology",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Austin Peay State University invites applications for an Engineering Technologist or Engineer at the rank of Assistant Professor. This is a full-time, 9-month tenure-track faculty position commencing July 30, 2027. The successful candidate will be able to develop and teach lower and upper division courses in the BS Engineering Technology program offerings of the department in the Mechatronics concentration. Candidate will be expected to engage in research and professional activities, contribute to the growth and development of the department through recruiting activities, serve on departmental and university committees, participate in assessment and evaluation, and a variety of other departmental activities. Austin Peay State University invites applications for an Engineering Technologist or Engineer at the rank of Assistant Professor. This is a full-time, 9-month tenure-track faculty position commencing July 30, 2027. The successful candidate will be able to develop and teach lower and upper division courses in the BS Engineering Technology program offerings of the department in the Mechatronics concentration. Candidate will be expected to engage in research and professional activities, contribute to the growth and development of the department through recruiting activities, serve on departmental and university committees, participate in assessment and evaluation, and a variety of other departmental activities. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teach any of the assigned courses in the Mechatronics concentration, including the major core lower and upper division courses, following ETAC of ABET requirements Manage complex capstone projects following ETAC of ABET requirements Be responsible for a minimum of 30 teaching load credits per academic year, 6 of which will be for advisement, research, committee work, etc. Establish productive student-oriented undergraduate research projects Assist in the development of any required new courses including online / hybrid courses that meet the needs of the Engineering Technology degree program. Demand and maintain high standards and expectations for all students. Implement teaching activities and a diversity of teaching techniques, procedures,and resources including application of technology. Develop and implement evaluation and assessment techniques that are appropriate for each course. Use multiple measures to assess student learning on a regular basis and provide frequent feedback to students relative to their performance. Be available and knowledgeable and demonstrate proficiency in the practice of academic advisement of students. Conduct appropriate research and scholarly/creative activity within the discipline. Demonstrate evidence of continuing professional development and growth by being suitably active in professional and community service. Exhibit motivation and initiative in keeping up-to-date and current in one’s curriculum area by reading/reviewing current scholarly or creative works in their field and by attending conferences, seminars, workshops, courses, and development activities sponsored by the University. Must be committed to the continuous improvement process of the program and contribute to program objectives, and outcomes to seek program accreditation by ETAC - ABET Serve effectively on committees and other appropriate functions that assist in University governance Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrate willingness and ability to work effectively with colleagues to support the mission of the institution and related academic units. Be willing to teach at times and places necessary to meet student needs. Be willing to adopt innovative teaching methods and delivery as appropriate. Possess the knowledge, talents and skills in the discipline to promote effective teaching. Demonstrate respect for the diverse learning needs of students. Demonstrate the ability to develop and implement curriculum objectives and content for courses offered and taught in one’s curriculum area. Physical Requirements A Master’s degree or higher in Engineering Technology or Engineering in Mechatronics or a closely related field including, but not limited to, Industrial Automation or Electrical Documented three years of relevant industrial experience preferred; Professional Registration (such as the P.E.) preferred; Ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff and the community; Evidence of good character, mature attitude and professional integrity; Mastery of common modern instrumental methods of analysis as pertaining to the candidate’s area of expertise; A background search will be required of the successful applicant. Applicant review will continue until the position is filled. Please refer all questions to facultyapplications@apsu.edu Required Documents Cover Letter Unofficial Transcript Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/401": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, BSN Program",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Applications are invited for a tenure track faculty position in the BSN program beginning July 30, 2027. The BSN program is comprised of two tracks; pre-licensure BSN and the RN- BSN Completion. The successful applicant will be expected to teach in the classroom as well as the clinical and lab/simulation setting, demonstrate a commitment to innovative and effective teaching and demonstrate evidence-based knowledge of area of discipline to be taught. Med-surgical nursing expertise is preferred. Applicant must be eligible for unencumbered RN licensure in TN. Rank and salary are dependent upon education and experience. Applications are invited for a tenure track faculty position in the BSN program beginning July 30, 2027. The BSN program is comprised of two tracks; pre-licensure BSN and the RN- BSN Completion. The successful applicant will be expected to teach in the classroom as well as the clinical and lab/simulation setting, demonstrate a commitment to innovative and effective teaching and demonstrate evidence-based knowledge of area of discipline to be taught. Med-surgical nursing expertise is preferred. Applicant must be eligible for unencumbered RN licensure in TN. Rank and salary are dependent upon education and experience. Primary Duties and Responsibilities · Demonstrate willingness and ability to work effectively with colleagues to support the mission of the institution and related academic units. · Be responsible for a maximum of 30 teaching load credits per academic year, 6 of which will be for advisement, research, committee work, etc. · Be willing to teach at times and places necessary to meet student needs. · Be willing to adopt innovative teaching methods and delivery as appropriate. · Possess the knowledge, talents and skills in the discipline to promote effective teaching. · Demonstrate respect for the diverse learning needs of students. · Demonstrate the ability to develop and implement curriculum objectives and content for courses offered and taught in one’s curriculum area. · Demand and maintain high standards and expectations for all students. · Implement teaching activities and a diversity of teaching techniques, procedures, and resources including application of technology. · Develop and implement evaluation and assessment techniques that are appropriate for each course. · Use multiple measures to assess student learning on a regular basis and provide frequent feedback to students relative to their performance. · Be available and knowledgeable and demonstrate proficiency in the practice of academic advisement of students. · Conduct appropriate research and scholarly/creative activity within the discipline. · Demonstrate evidence of continuing professional development and growth by being suitably active in professional and community service. · Exhibit motivation and initiative in keeping up-to-date and current in one’s curriculum area by reading/reviewing current scholarly or creative works in their field and by attending conferences, seminars, workshops, courses, and development activities sponsored by the University. · Serve effectively on committees and other appropriate functions that assist in University governance. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities · Demonstrate teamwork and collaborative skills. · Demonstrate innovation in teaching. · Demonstrate knowledge of teaching assessment and evaluation. · Demonstrate commitment to ongoing scholarly development. · Demonstrate effective communication skills. Required Minimum Qualifications · Baccalaureate degree in nursing (CCNE) Graduate degree in nursing or other healthcare graduate degree · B accalaureate teaching experience preferred · have clinical experience; minimum 3 years of practice experience · Doctoral degree in nursing required by tenure. · Candidate must be eligible for unencumbered RN licensure in Tennessee. · A background search will be required of the successful candidate. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/402": {
      "title": "Anatomy & Physiology Instructor",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Austin Peay State University invites applications for a full-time 9-month instructor position (three-year, renewable, nontenure contract role) for the Department of Biology. This position is face-to-face/in-person teaching starting July 30, 2027. Teaching may take place at the Clarksville and/or Ft. Campbell campuses. There may be opportunities for summer teaching. Austin Peay State University invites applications for a full-time 9-month instructor position (three-year, renewable, nontenure contract role) for the Department of Biology. This position is face-to-face/in-person teaching starting July 30, 2027. Teaching may take place at the Clarksville and/or Ft. Campbell campuses. There may be opportunities for summer teaching. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Teach 24 workload credits (WLCs) per academic year (Fall and Spring semesters) or approximately 12 workload credits per semester (roughly two lectures and two labs each semester). Coordinate BIOL 2010/2011 Human Anatomy and Physiology I and BIOL 2020/2021 Human Anatomy and Physiology II courses, including keeping courses updated and current to meet departmental needs; maintaining common online platform courses (D2L learning module and Pearson’s Mastering A&P), syllabi, outlines, and other course materials to be shared with all Human Anatomy & Physiology instructors; completing and submitting general education assessments and other assessment activities of Human Anatomy and Physiology I and II, and making changes as needed based on data collected; and carrying out other duties as needed to fulfill course coordinator role. Supervise Graduate Teaching Assistants (GTAs) and student worker s who are teaching and prepping Human Anatomy and Physiology I and II lab sections; including working with GTAs to ensure that they are prepared to teach Human Anatomy & Physiology lab sections; serving as instructor of record for lab sections taught by GTAs who do not meet instructor of record requirements; ensuring all syllabus, gradebook, and grade/attendance submission requirements are met for all GTA taught sections; evaluating GTAs and adjuncts teaching A&P, and managing issues related to Human Anatomy and Physiology I and II labs, including student related issues. Serve on/chair Departmental, College, or University Committees that are Relevant to Position Work with the Faculty and Staff to promote recruitment, retention, and overall student success and to support departmental initiatives and success, including participation in departmental and other required meetings. Other duties assigned by the Chair, Dean, or APSU Administration Physical Requirements Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Required Minimum Qualifications - Master's degree or higher in Biology or related field. - Ph.D. in Biology, Anatomy and Physiology, or related field preferred. - Demonstrated success as a teacher with three or more years of experience teaching anatomy and physiology. - A background search will be required of the successful applicant. Special Instructions to Applicants Each applicant must include the names and contact information for three references, one of which must be from your most recent or current employer, with your application materials. Many people add this to the end of the CV. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/404": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Teaching & Learning",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The College of Education is seeking candidates for a tenure-track position for Education Generalist. The teaching assignment will include Education Generalist courses at the undergraduate and graduate level. There is the possibility of teaching on-line, on ground and off campus courses. Position is scheduled to begin July 30, 2027. The College of Education at Austin Peay State University provides teacher training in an environment that provides opportunities for students and faculty to work and learn together. Small classes provide opportunities for students and faculty to establish relationships that will last throughout a student’s academic career. Teaching and advising are valued skills and weighed equally with research in the evaluation process. Salary is competitive and commensurate with education and experience. The College of Education is seeking candidates for a tenure-track position for Education Generalist. The teaching assignment will include Education Generalist courses at the undergraduate and graduate level. There is the possibility of teaching on-line, on ground and off campus courses. Position is scheduled to begin July 30, 2027. The College of Education at Austin Peay State University provides teacher training in an environment that provides opportunities for students and faculty to work and learn together. Small classes provide opportunities for students and faculty to establish relationships that will last throughout a student’s academic career. Teaching and advising are valued skills and weighed equally with research in the evaluation process. Salary is competitive and commensurate with education and experience. Primary Duties and Responsibilities -Teach education courses in the general education curriculum (i.e. foundations of education, classroom management, etc) with preferred teaching experience in educational psychology and/or science education and/or assessment and/or instructional technology. -Mentor pre-service teacher candidates who are seeking a professional teaching license. -Serve on COE committees. -Active engagement in research and scholarly presentations of research. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred educational coursework and teaching experience in educational psychology and/or science education and/or assessment and/or instructional technology Required Minimum Qualifications -An earned doctorate/terminal degree in the field of Education -Demonstrated record of, or potential for, scholarship and publication -A minimum of three years of successful teaching experience in preK-12 public education in the U.S. is required. -Evidence of excellence in teaching, potential for scholarly research, achievement in professional endeavors, interpersonal skills, sensitivity to diversity, and ability to relate to local constituencies. -A background search will be required of the successful applicant. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/409": {
      "title": "Adjunct  Part-time Instructor (Pool) - Graduate Strategic Leadership",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Department of Leadership is seeking to expand the pool of part-time, temporary, adjunct instructors to teach online graduate-level courses as opportunities arise within the Master of Science in Leadership program. Potential courses for adjunct instruction include: LDSP 5050 Values & Ethics in Leadership, LDSP 5060 Communication Skills for Leaders, LDSP 5140 Influence & Persuasion, LDSP 5200 Organizational Culture, Politics, & Change, LDSP 5210 Leading in a Global Society, LDSP 5560 Small Group Leadership, LDSP 5700 Conflict Management & Negotiation, and courses related to other Leadership sub-topics as needed. Each of these courses is designed to equip graduate students with in-depth knowledge about the behavioral science of leadership and provide opportunities to apply that knowledge to real-world situations through directed readings, written assignments, course discussions, and more. The Department of Leadership is seeking to expand the pool of part-time, temporary, adjunct instructors to teach online graduate-level courses as opportunities arise within the Master of Science in Leadership program. Potential courses for adjunct instruction include: LDSP 5050 Values & Ethics in Leadership, LDSP 5060 Communication Skills for Leaders, LDSP 5140 Influence & Persuasion, LDSP 5200 Organizational Culture, Politics, & Change, LDSP 5210 Leading in a Global Society, LDSP 5560 Small Group Leadership, LDSP 5700 Conflict Management & Negotiation, and courses related to other Leadership sub-topics as needed. Each of these courses is designed to equip graduate students with in-depth knowledge about the behavioral science of leadership and provide opportunities to apply that knowledge to real-world situations through directed readings, written assignments, course discussions, and more. Candidates should indicate which course(s) or specialty area(s) they are most interested in and qualified to teach in their cover letter. Previous experience teaching in a fully online environment is preferred. Primary Duties and Responsibilities - Teach online courses in the Master of Science in Leadership program. Physical Requirements Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to move objects. Required Minimum Qualifications - Doctorate in Leadership or related area; - Significant professional experience in the specific area related to the course; - A background search will be required of the successful applicant. Required Documents 1. Cover Letter 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. Unofficial Transcript Optional Documents 1. Letter of Recommendation 1 2. Letter of Recommendation 2 3. Letter of Recommendation 3 The number of adjunct instructors hired varies from semester to semester, depending upon the needs of the department. Each applicant must include the names and contact information for three references, one of which must be from your most recent or current employer, with your application materials. Many people add this to the end of the CV/Resume. If you would like to additionally attach Letters of Recommendation to your online application, letters must be dated one year or less from the date of your application. Letters of recommendation may be sent by email to “ facultyapplications@apsu.edu ” or hard copy to “Austin Peay State University, Human Resources Dept., PO Box 4507, Clarksville, TN 37044” with your name and desired position clearly indicated after your online application is completed. If granted an interview, unofficial transcripts will be required of applicants and official transcripts will be required of the selected candidate before the candidate will be offered a position. It is highly recommended that you attach unofficial transcripts in PDF format to your online application. You will not be able to attach your letters of recommendation, unofficial transcripts or any other supplemental document(s) nor modify your application after it has been submitted. Please refer all questions to facultyapplications@apsu.edu "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/362": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Leadership",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Nominations and applications are invited for the position of Assistant Professor of Leadership. The area of specialization is open, however, experience or interest in the area of Community Leadership, and Inclusive Leadership is desirable. This is a full-time, tenure-track position to begin July 30, 2027 and will serve graduate and undergraduate programs in the Department of Leadership. The person hired for this position will have the opportunity to manage a dynamic and innovative curriculum in the role of Graduate Program Coordinator starting in the 2nd year of employment. Nominations and applications are invited for the position of Assistant Professor of Leadership . The area of specialization is open, however experience or interest in the area of Community Leadership, and Inclusive Leadership is desirable . This is a full-time, tenure-track position to begin July 30, 2027 and will serve graduate and undergraduate programs in the Department of Leadership. The person hired for this position will have the opportunity to manage a dynamic and innovative curriculum in the role of Graduate Program Coordinator starting in the 2 nd year of employment. The Department of Leadership is a collegial environment housed within the College of Behavioral and Health Sciences. Our mission is to offer online academic programs that address leadership-related theory, research, and practice grounded in the social and behavioral sciences, thereby helping students develop the leadership competencies needed to become formal or informal leaders and advance their careers in varied employment settings. At the undergraduate level, we offer a Bachelor of Science in Leadership along with a minor in Leadership Science. At the graduate level, we offer a Master of Science in Leadership with three concentrations: Strategic Leadership, Community Leadership, and Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion. The department also offers five graduate certificate programs, including: Community & Organizational Leadership; Conflict Resolution & Negotiation; Diversity, Equity, & Inclusion in the Workplace; Grant Writing; Leading Organizational Change. The department is also involved in co-curricular efforts, including sponsorship of APSU’s Chapter of the National Society of Leadership and Success . Teaching responsibilities may include undergraduate and graduate courses in leadership theory, organizational leadership, research methods, community leadership, inclusive leadership, strategic leadership, and other related areas. The successful candidate will hold weekly, in-person office hours and will be assigned to teach both hybrid and online courses. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Starting in Year Two, serve as departmental Graduate Coordinator and commit to all responsibilities associated with that role. Be willing to adopt innovative teaching methods and delivery as appropriate. Possess the knowledge, talents, and skills to promote effective teaching in the discipline of Leadership. Demonstrate respect for the diverse learning needs of students. Demonstrate the ability to develop and implement curriculum objectives and content for courses offered and taught in one’s curriculum area. Maintain high standards and expectations for all students. Use multiple measures to assess student learning on a regular basis and provide frequent feedback to students relative to their performance. Be available, knowledgeable and demonstrate proficiency in the practice of academic advisement of students. Conduct appropriate research and scholarly/creative activity within the discipline. Demonstrate evidence of continuing professional development and exhibit a willingness to engage in service to the department, college, university, and broader community. More information about the department and its programs can be found on our website: https://www.apsu.edu/leadership/ . Required Qualifications Earned doctorate in Leadership or related social and behavioral science field from a regionally accredited program. ABD will be considered if the doctorate will be completed by July 30, 2027. Documented evidence of ability in a teaching assignment. Documented evidence of scholarly and creative achievement within the discipline of Leadership and/or Leadership-adjacent disciplines appropriate for the rank of Assistant Professor. (Departmental Retention, Tenure, and Promotion Criteria available online here .) Documented evidence of university service and professional contributions and activities appropriate for that of an Assistant Professor. Preferred Qualifications: Strong evidence of research capabilities at the R1 level. Evidence of graduate level program management, recruitment and teaching. Application Procedure Applicants should submit the following: 1. Letter of application addressing interest in the position and qualifications 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Three Letters of Recommendation and/or names and contact information of 3 professional references (can be listed on CV) 4. Teaching Philosophy and Experience "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/363": {
      "title": "Instructor - Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Department of Criminal Justice at Austin Peay State University invites applications for an on-ground instructor position starting July 30, 2027. This instructor position entails approximately nine months of full-time service and is a three-year, renewable position. The Department of Criminal Justice at Austin Peay State University invites applications for an on-ground instructor position starting July 30, 2027. This instructor position entails approximately nine months of full-time service and is a three-year, renewable position. The Department of Criminal Justice currently offers bachelor's and master of science degrees in criminal justice, each with an optional concentration in homeland security. Additionally, the department houses a bachelor’s degree in national security studies. The program enrolls about 400 undergraduate majors per year and has approximately 60 in our graduate cohorts. The Department of Criminal Justice offers its courses through diverse delivery methods, including face-to-face, online, and hybrid/blended formats. The successful candidate will be able to teach courses in all modalities. The Department of Criminal Justice is among the University’s fastest growing. The position’s responsibilities include teaching courses as assigned by the chair. Courses may require teaching at the Fort Campbell Center. Additionally, the successful candidate will advise students and participate in relevant service to the university, community, and discipline. More information about the department is available at http://www.apsu.edu/criminal-justice. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will: • Teach four to five courses (graduate and undergraduate level) per academic semester as assigned by the chair • Advise majors as needed • Provide service, including, but not limited to, departmental, college, and/or university committee work • Faculty may teach during the summer semesters for additional compensation (subject to performance and availability) Required Qualifications: • One of the following: Ph.D. in criminal justice or criminology, a J.D., a Master’s degree in law/legal studies, or a Master’s degree in criminal justice with significant experience in courts/law. • A background search will be required of the successful applicant. Desired Qualifications • An ability to teach a wide range of law-focused criminal justice courses • Experience teaching across a variety of delivery methods (online, hybrid, face-to-face, etc.) You should include in your application the following: a letter of application highlighting relevant experience as it pertains to the position, a curriculum vitae, copies of all undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and a list of three references with your application. Initial review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026 . Applicant review will continue until the position is filled. Please refer all questions to facultyapplications@apsu.edu or the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Christopher Wright, wrightc@apsu.edu. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/371": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Counseling Psychology-PsyD",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Department of Psychological Science and Counseling at Austin Peay State University (APSU) seeks to fill two tenure-track faculty positions in Counseling Psychology with a start date of July 30, 2027. This position will serve our American Psychological Association (APA) accredited PsyD program in Counseling Psychology. The program offers a generalist track as well as a concentration in Serving Military Personnel, Veterans, and their Families. The persons hired for this position will have a unique opportunity to help shape an innovative, forward-looking doctoral training program in health service psychology. Strong candidates will have a deep commitment to the foundational values that characterize the field of counseling psychology: a holistic, contextual, strengths-based approach to intervention; an emphasis on integrating science and practice; and a steadfast commitment to culturally responsive practice and social justice. The Department of Psychological Science and Counseling at Austin Peay State University (APSU) seeks to fill two tenure-track faculty positions in Counseling Psychology with a start date of July 30, 2027. This position will serve our American Psychological Association (APA) accredited PsyD program in Counseling Psychology. The program offers a generalist track as well as a concentration in Serving Military Personnel, Veterans, and their Families. The persons hired for this position will have a unique opportunity to help shape an innovative, forward-looking doctoral training program in health service psychology. Strong candidates will have a deep commitment to the foundational values that characterize the field of counseling psychology: a holistic, contextual, strengths-based approach to intervention; an emphasis on integrating science and practice; and a steadfast commitment to culturally responsive practice and social justice. A d octorate ( Psy D or PhD) in Counseling Psy chology (preferred) or Clinical Psy chology (acceptable) from an APA-accredited program is required. Preferred candidates will be licensed as a psy chologist HSP or be license-eligible in TN within 1 year of hire. Support is available for postdoctoral hours accrual. Clinical, teaching, and research areas are open, but interest and expertise in health psychology, consultation, ethics, geropsychology, cognitive and intellectual assessment, counseling children and adolescents, and/or counseling couples and families, as well as interest and/or experience working with military populations is d esirable but not required. All APSU faculty are expected to be engaged in university and community service, and scholarly activities. Faculty in the PsyD program also provide clinical supervision and consultation to doctoral students engaged in clinical work. The university has plentiful funding opportunities to help support research, teaching, and professional d evelopment. Additional information about the position is found here: https://www.apsu.edu/psychology/psyd/ . The program is housed in the new state-of-the-art Health Professions Building, which includes an in-house clinic that serves as both a training facility and a site for providing mental health services to the campus and community. The Department of Psychological Science and Counseling is a diverse, dynamic, and collegial environment that, in addition to the PsyD program, is home to a large undergraduate program in psychological science, a Master of Science program in Industrial and Organizational Psychology (MSIO), a Master of Science program in Counseling, and a graduate certificate program in Academic Advising. For more information about the d epartment, visit: http://www.apsu.edu/ psy chology/index.php . The d epartment is housed within the College of Behavioral and Health Sciences, which affords rich opportunities for interdisciplinary collaborations. Some examples of recent and ongoing college collaborations include a grant-funded research and intervention project aimed at supporting student-veteran transitions to college, a grant-funded project focused on student mental health and wellness, a juvenile justice mentorship project, and a working group focused on trauma-informed pedagogy. For additional information about APSU including our mission and vision please visit: https://www.apsu.edu/about-apsu/index.php Primary D uties and Responsibilities Demonstrate the ability to work effectively with colleagues to support the mission of the institution and related academic units. Carry a minimum teaching load of 30 credits per academic year, including 6 credits for advisement, research, committee work, and related faculty responsibilities, with the potential for summer teaching assignments (with additional compensation) as the program operates year-round. Teach at times and places necessary to meet student needs. Provide clinical supervision and consultation to students at the departmental clinic and outside practicum sites. Employ innovative teaching methods and instructional delivery approaches, as appropriate. Possess the knowledge, talents and skills in the d iscipline to promote effective teaching. D emonstrate respect for the varied learning needs of students. D evelop and implement curriculum objectives and content for assigned courses. D emand and maintain high standards and expectations for all students. Implement a variety of evidence-based teaching strategies, instructional techniques, and educational technologies. Provide guidance and support for students’ dissertation research and scholarly projects. D evelop and implement evaluation and assessment methods for each course. Use multiple measures to assess student learning on a regular basis and provide frequent feedback to students relative to their performance. Provide effective academic advising and demonstrate proficiency in supporting students' academic and professional development. Conduct appropriate research and scholarly/creative activity within the d iscipline. Effectively utilize the materials and resources of the Felix G. Woodward Library in teaching, scholarship, and service. Demonstrate ongoing professional growth through active participation in professional organizations, continuing education, and community engagement. Maintain current disciplinary expertise through engagement with scholarly literature and participation in conferences, workshops, seminars, and university-sponsored professional development activities. Serve effectively on departmental, college, and university committees and contribute to shared governance. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Pedagogical Skills in Counseling Psy chology Knowledge base in Counseling Psy chology Knowledge and Skills in Research Methods Required Minimum Qualifications Earned PhD or Psy D from an accredited institution in Counseling Psychology or Clinical Psychology. ABD considered if conferred before July 30, 2027. D ocumented evidence of ability in academic assignments and/or scholarly and creative achievement, and/or professional contributions and activities. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/378": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Psychological Science, Clinical",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Nominations and applications are invited for the position of Assistant Professor, Psychological Science area of specialization is open. This is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track position to begin July 30, 2027. Nominations and applications are invited for the position of Assistant Professor , Psychological Science area of specialization is open . This is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track position to begin July 30, 2027. The Department of Psychological Science and Counseling is a diverse, dynamic, and collegial environment that is home to a large undergraduate program in psychological science, a Master of Science program in Industrial and Organizational Psychology (MSIO), a Master of Science program in Counseling, and a PsyD program specializing in working with military families . For more information about the department, visit: http://www.apsu.edu/psychology/index.php . The department is housed within the College of Behavioral and Health Sciences which affords rich opportunities for interdisciplinary collaborations. Some examples of recent and ongoing college collaborations include a grant-funded research and intervention project aimed at supporting student veteran transitions to college, a grant-funded project focused on student mental health and wellness, a juvenile justice mentorship project, and a working group focusing on trauma-informed pedagogy. Austin Peay State University is located in Clarksville, TN, which Money Magazine rated number 1 in its 2019 Best Places to Live rankings: https://clarksvillenow.com/local/clarksville-named-best-place-to-live-by-money-magazine/ . Clarksville is a vibrant, diverse community with a low cost of living, and easy interstate access to nearby Nashville. Clarksville is centrally located in the region, with Memphis, Louisville, Atlanta, St. Louis, Chicago, Cincinnati, Indianapolis, New Orleans, and many other major cities a day’s drive away. For additional information about APSU, including our mission and vision, please visit: https://www.apsu.edu/about-apsu/index.php Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teaching responsibilities in our recently revamped curriculum will include a range of undergraduate courses in the Bachelor of Science program, including PSYC 1030 – Introduction to Psychology and courses in the selected candidate’s specialty area. Preference will be given to candidates who can contribute to one or more of the following areas: introduction to psychopathology, introduction to clinical neuroscience, and/or learning and behavioral disorders. Follow the link for a curriculum overview and a list of departmental undergraduate courses . The departmental teaching load is 12 hours each semester, which can include credit for leading research teams comprised of undergraduate researchers. Summer teaching opportunities are available. Research activity is required for this position, and scholarship activities involving undergraduates will be encouraged. The Department of Psychological Science currently has a variety of laboratory spaces and a collaborative developmental and play observation/lab space. In addition, the university has funding opportunities to help support research and teaching equipment expenses. Candidates who demonstrate a strong interest in undergraduate education and involving undergraduates in research, in contributing to general education teaching and advising, and in departmental service are preferred. Applicant review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. More information about the department and its programs can be found on our website: https://www.apsu.edu/psychology/ . Required Qualifications A Ph.D. in Psychology is required, with the area of specialization open. ABD will be considered if the Ph.D. will be completed by July 30, 2027. Screening of applications will continue until position is filled. Applicants should submit the following: 1. Letter of application addressing interest in the position, qualifications, and a statement of research interests 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Three Letters of Recommendation and/or names and contact information of 3 professional references (can be listed on CV) 4. Teaching Philosophy and Experience Optional: 1. Transcript "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/384": {
      "title": "University Librarian & Executive Director of Library Services",
      "description": "JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The University Librarian & Executive Director of Library Services serves as the chief administrator and strategic leader of the Felix G. Woodward Library at Austin Peay State University. Reporting to the Provost and Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs, the University Librarian & Executive Director serves as a member of the Provost’s Leadership Team and provides visionary, collaborative, and innovative leadership for the University’s library services, resources, personnel, facilities, technologies, and learning environments. The University Librarian & Executive Director of Library Services serves as the chief administrator and strategic leader of the Felix G. Woodward Library at Austin Peay State University. Reporting to the Provost and Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs, the University Librarian & Executive Director serves as a member of the Provost’s Leadership Team and provides visionary, collaborative, and innovative leadership for the University’s library services, resources, personnel, facilities, technologies, and learning environments. The University Librarian & Executive Director is responsible for leading an experienced team of over 25 library faculty and staff; managing the overall library budget of ~3.3M; and planning, implementing, assessing, and continuously improving library programs, collections, services, technologies, and spaces. The position provides visionary leadership for key service areas, including access and discovery, collections and resource management, library technology and digital services, research and instruction, and University archives and special collections. The University Librarian & Executive Director represents Woodward Library across the University, within the Association of College and Research Libraries (ACRL), and throughout the local and regional community. This position is expected to position the library as a dynamic academic hub that advances APSU’s mission, supports student success, strengthens faculty research and scholarship, promotes equitable access to information, and contributes meaningfully to the intellectual and cultural life of the University. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Provide strategic, forward-thinking leadership for the Felix G. Woodward Library, ensuring that library services, collections, technologies, staffing, and spaces align with the University’s mission, academic priorities, enrollment goals, student success initiatives, and strategic plan. Lead and support library faculty and staff through a culture grounded in transparent communication, collaboration, collegiality and mutual respect. Provide administrative leadership and management for all library service units and related library operations that support innovation, accountability, and continuous improvement. Develop and implement visionary goals for the library that support teaching, learning, and research goals of the university. Manage the library’s budget, personnel resources, physical facilities, digital infrastructure, collections, and operational priorities in a strategic, sustainable, and data-informed manner. Collaborate with academic leadership and divisional campus partners to advance the library’s role in student success and ensure that library resources and services are integrated into the academic life of the University, creating modern, accessible, student-centered physical and virtual library environments. Lead the continued development of a modern, accessible, student-centered physical and virtual library environments at a public university Provide leadership in the development, evaluation, preservation, and accessibility of print, digital, archival, and special collections that support APSU’s academic programs, research priorities, and institutional history. Promote the library as a vibrant intellectual, cultural, and academic commons for students, faculty, staff, alumni, and the broader Clarksville-Montgomery County community. Lead the library in responding effectively to emerging trends in academic librarianship, including artificial intelligence, digital learning, open science, evolving integrated library systems, metadata and discovery tools, accessibility standards, and new models of information access. Oversee accreditation and external compliance of the library in consultation with the Associate Director of Library Services. Advance a culture of inclusion and belonging, maintaining a welcoming library environment for all students, faculty, staff, alumni, and community members. Recruit, mentor, evaluate, and support the professional growth of library faculty and staff, ensuring that personnel have opportunities to develop expertise in contemporary library practices, technologies, student support, and academic engagement. Represent the Woodward Library on the Provost’s Leadership Team, University Library Advisory Committee, and the Woodward Library Society Board, as well as in professional organizations, community partnerships, and other internal and external forums, as appropriate, cultivating relationships that support library initiatives. Cultivate partnerships with alumni, donors, foundations, corporate partners, community organizations, and grant-making entities to support library priorities, special initiatives, collections, facilities, technology, and student-centered programming. Ensure that library policies and procedures are current, user-centered, equitable, and aligned with professional academic library standards and best practices. Represent the University and Woodward Library in professional organizations, consortia, community partnerships, state and regional library networks, and other external forums. Perform other related duties as assigned or requested. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities A proven record of success as a collaborative leader and transparent communicator with the ability to develop and convey a compelling vision for the role of the academic library in a changing higher education environment. Demonstrated knowledge of contemporary issues facing higher education and academic libraries, including intellectual freedom, academic privacy, information /media literacy, scholarly communication, open access, artificial intelligence, digital preservation, and equitable access to library resources and spaces. A transparent, collaborative, and participatory leadership style that fosters trust, shared purpose, accountability, innovation, and collegiality among library faculty and staff. Demonstrated ability to manage complex budgets and align financial decisions with institutional priorities, and long-term sustainability. Demonstrated experience in library assessment, data-informed decision-making, strategic planning, and accreditation support. A demonstrated commitment to inclusion, belonging, and for all library users of resources, services, and spaces. Commitment to understanding and addressing the library needs of all undergraduate and graduate students (including traditional, post-traditional, first-generation, and military-affiliated), recognizing a variety of experiences, identities, and perspectives. The ability to build effective working relationships with faculty, staff, and administrators, alumni, and community partners to advance the mission of the library. Experience supporting faculty teaching, research, and curriculum development, and the integration of library resources into academic programs. Ability to foster a positive and productive work environment that supports professional development, faculty and staff engagement, shared governance, and high-quality service. Demonstrated ability to promote the library’s value and impact through advocacy, communication, outreach, assessment, and relationship-building. Experience supporting fundraising, grant opportunities, and development efforts that advance library priorities. Strong communication, interpersonal, organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills. Maintain awareness of national and regional trends in higher education and academic libraries, using that knowledge to guide strategic planning, innovation, resource allocation, and service development. A deep commitment to academic excellence, student success, faculty support, public service, and the mission of Austin Peay State University. Minimum Required Qualifications An ALA-Accredited Master of Library Science or Master's or equivalent degree. A strong record of achievement in the areas of research, teaching, and service with evidence meriting appointment as the rank of tenured associate or full professor within the Felix G. Woodward Library. Minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible leadership experience in an academic library, preferably within a public university or comprehensive four-year higher education setting. Demonstrated experience supervising, mentoring, and evaluating library faculty, professional staff and/or support staff. Demonstrated experience managing library operations, services, budgets, personnel, collections, technologies, and/or facilities. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/385": {
      "title": "Dean, Honors College",
      "description": "JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Dean of the Honors College serves as the senior academic and administrative leader for Austin Peay State University’s Honors College. Reporting to the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs, the Dean provides visionary leadership, strategic direction, and academic oversight for the Honors College and serves as the chief advocate for honors students, faculty, programs, and initiatives across the university. The Dean is responsible for advancing a honors experience that promotes a distinctive curriculum grounded in high-impact practices and innovative teaching, undergraduate research and creative inquiry, global learning, community engagement, internships, leadership development, competitive fellowships, and other experiential learning opportunities. Aligning the Honors College’s academic priorities with institutional goals and national best practices, the Dean will lead efforts to strengthen the Honors College as an academic home for high-achieving students and as a univer The Dean of the Honors College serves as the senior academic and administrative leader for Austin Peay State University’s Honors College. Reporting to the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs, the Dean provides visionary leadership, strategic direction, and academic oversight for the Honors College and serves as the chief advocate for honors students, faculty, programs, and initiatives across the university. The Dean is responsible for advancing a honors experience that promotes a distinctive curriculum grounded in high-impact practices and innovative teaching, undergraduate research and creative inquiry, global learning, community engagement, internships, leadership development, competitive fellowships, and other experiential learning opportunities. Aligning the Honors College’s academic priorities with institutional goals and national best practices, the Dean will lead efforts to strengthen the Honors College as an academic home for high-achieving students and as a university-wide catalyst for innovation, student success, and distinguished achievement. The Dean will oversee the Honors College budget, programs, assessment, faculty, staff, and student leadership structures, while working collaboratively with academic colleges, departments, Admissions, Advancement, Government Relations, Student Affairs, and external partners. The Dean will also represent Austin Peay State University in national honors networks and lead recruitment, fundraising, and development efforts for the Honors College. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Provide strategic vision, academic leadership, and administrative oversight for the Honors College. Report directly to the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs and serve as a member of the university’s academic leadership team. Oversee Honors College programs, operations, budget, faculty, staff, student initiatives, and assessment processes. Develop, implement, and evaluate Honors College policies, procedures, academic standards, and curricular expectations. Lead the development of Honors courses, seminars, interdisciplinary and transdisciplinary learning opportunities, and other academic experiences that support Honors education. Work collaboratively with academic deans, department chairs, faculty, and academic programs to expand and coordinate Honors course offerings across the university. Represent Austin Peay State University in National honors networks and related organizations, including the National Collegiate Honors Council, Council of Undergraduate Research, National Association of Fellowships Advisors, and other such organizations. Provide oversight for the awarding and recognition of Honors degrees, Honors distinctions, and related student achievements. Supervise and provide leadership for Honors College personnel and affiliated roles, including the Associate Dean, Director of Undergraduate Research and Innovative Learning, Director of Global Education and Competitive Fellowships, Director of Community Engaged Learning, Faculty Fellows, Faculty-in-Residence, communications staff, administrative staff, and student leadership groups. Support and guide the work of the Associate Dean in Honors course scheduling, Honors course development, assessment, student success outcomes, internship placement, and retention and graduation strategies. Support the Director of Undergraduate Research and Innovative Learning in expanding undergraduate research, experiential learning, internships, externships, cooperative education, and career-connected academic opportunities. Support the Director of Global Education and Competitive Fellowships in advancing study abroad, study away, faculty and student exchanges, Washington Center Internships, and competitive fellowships such as Fulbright, Rhodes, Truman, Goldwater, Gilman, and related programs. Support the Director of Community Engaged Learning in advancing service learning, community-engaged learning, the President’s Emerging Leaders Program, and other high-impact practices connected to campus and community needs. Provide oversight for Faculty Fellows and Faculty-in-Residence who teach Honors seminars, mentor students, support Honors theses and undergraduate research, and lead co-curricular initiatives. Engage and advise Honors Student Council and Honors College Ambassadors to support student leadership, recruitment, mentoring, programming, and peer engagement. Develop and maintain strong partnerships with faculty, staff, alumni, donors, community organizations, national programs, and external stakeholders. Use data, assessment, and student success outcomes to evaluate Honors College effectiveness and guide continuous improvement. Promote a culture of academic excellence, innovation, belonging, leadership, civic engagement, and student achievement within the Honors College. Perform other duties as assigned by the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of Honors education, high-impact practices and experiential learning, , student leadership development, and academic excellence initiatives. Knowledge of contemporary trends in Honors education, higher education, student success, retention, persistence, graduation strategies, and post-graduate preparation. Strong understanding of academic program development, curriculum design, Honors course development, and interdisciplinary and transdisciplinary learning. Ability to provide visionary leadership and strategic direction for a growing Honors College. Ability to work collaboratively with academic deans, department chairs, faculty, staff, students, alumni, donors, and external partners. Strong administrative, organizational, budgeting, planning, and assessment skills. Ability to lead faculty and staff, build effective teams, and foster a collaborative and student-centered culture. Ability to advocate effectively for Honors students, Honors faculty, and the mission of the Honors College. Strong communication, public speaking, writing, and interpersonal skills. Ability to lead recruitment and retention strategies for academically talented and high-achieving students. Ability to cultivate philanthropic support, engage donors, and develop external partnerships that advance Honors College priorities. Ability to represent the university professionally in local, regional, national, and international settings. Knowledge of competitive fellowship and scholarship programs and the role they play in elevating student achievement and institutional reputation. Ability to use data and assessment to evaluate student outcomes, program effectiveness, and continuous improvement. Commitment to academic excellence, student success, innovation, leadership development, community engagement, and the mission of Austin Peay State University. Required Minimum Qualifications An earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution in an academic discipline appropriate for appointment as a tenured faculty member at Austin Peay State University. A record of teaching, scholarship, and service sufficient to merit appointment at the rank of Professor Demonstrated experience in academic leadership, which may include service as a department chair, associate dean, program director, honors program leader, center director, or comparable academic administrative role. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/398": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Category: Athletic Coaching, Training and Program Management JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Assistant Athletic Trainer is responsible for the care, prevention, and rehabilitation of injuries and/or illnesses to Austin Peay State University athletes as well as others as referred by a team physician. The Assistant Athletic Trainer is responsible for the care, prevention, and rehabilitation of injuries and/or illnesses to Austin Peay State University athletes as well as others as referred by a team physician. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Prevention, treatment, and rehabilitation for all physically active individuals, including Austin Peay State University athletes and others as referred by a team physician, men and women. Attend assigned team(s) practice sessions and contests, home and away. Travel with sports teams as directed. Drug testing of athletes. Attend home contests for all sponsored sports and away contests as assigned, to include nights, holidays and weekends. Responsible for Automated External Defibrillator(s) registration /regular maintenance. Follow guidelines as established by the Head Athletic Trainer for athletic training, practice set-up, and game set-up. Assist with daily coverage of athletic training facility. Supervise and follow established rules of the NCAA , University, Athletics Department and Athletic Training Department. Must possess a complete knowledge of and be in compliance with all NCAA and ASUN rules related to this position. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to interact in an effective and appropriate manner with diverse populations, the University community and the public. Must have a thorough knowledge of human anatomy, treating injuries with the modalities available and rehabilitation techniques to be used after an injury is sustained by the athlete. Competency in handling supplies. Ability to function within the existing inventory and budget. Ability to keep current and complete records/notes on individuals seen while performing duties of the job. Ability to respond to supervision and abide by and follow established rules of the NCAA , University, Athletics Department, and Athletic Training Department. Must be certified by the National Athletic Trainers’ Association and must maintain certificate during the course of employment. Must be licensed by the Tennessee Board of Medical Examiners within the first six months of employment and must maintain certificate during the course of employment. Physical Requirements Medium work – Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Required Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. NATABOC certification and eligibility for a Tennessee Athletic Trainer’s License. Tennessee license must be obtained within the first six (6) months of employment. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/359": {
      "title": "Director, University Budget",
      "description": "Category: Finance, Budget, and Planning JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Budget Director is responsible for the preparation and submission of all University budgets to the APSU Board of Trustees, the Tennessee Board of Regents, and the Tennessee Higher Education Commission. Executes the budget planning process for each fiscal year. Processes budget revisions throughout the year. Provides training, ad-hoc reports, and analyses. The Budget Director is responsible for the preparation and submission of all University budgets to the APSU Board of Trustees, the Tennessee Board of Regents, and the Tennessee Higher Education Commission. Executes the budget planning process for each fiscal year. Processes budget revisions throughout the year. Provides training, ad-hoc reports, and analyses. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Maintain the University approved position salary budgets. Prepare the three financial budgets per year (original, revised, and estimated) and two personnel budgets (original and revised) to be approved by the APSU Board of Trustees, Tennessee Board of Regents, and the Tennessee Higher Education Commission. Plan, communicate, and execute the annual fee proposal and budget request Process revenue and expense budget revisions. Provide budget analyses and projections to be used by University administration for critical resource allocation planning. Provide ad-hoc reports, schedules, and analysis as requested. Answer general budget questions and provide training to faculty and staff. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong proficiency in Excel Strong computing, organization, analytical, and critical thinking skills. Demonstrated knowledge of finance and budget management policies and procedures; Required Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Accounting, or Finance. Minimum of four (4) years experience in Budgeting, Planning, reporting, and/or analysis. Excellent communication and customer service skills. Physical Requirements Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry,push, pull or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/357": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Annual Giving",
      "description": "Category: University Advancement JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States As Austin Peay State University approaches its centennial, we are seeking an Assistant Director of Annual Giving to support the university's growing culture of philanthropy. As institutional priorities evolve, this position may also be assigned additional fundraising responsibilities in support of the university's overall philanthropic goals. The Assistant Director of Annual Giving is responsible for the planning, implementation, and execution of annual giving initiatives designed to increase donor participation and annual philanthropic support. This position manages university-wide annual giving campaigns, partners with academic and administrative units, and collaborates with colleagues across the Division of Alumni, Engagement and Philanthropy to achieve annual fundraising goals. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Annual Giving Management (70%) Develop and execute annual giving initiatives that increase donor participation and philanthropic support. Lead the planning and execution of university-wide annual giving campaigns, including Govs Give, GOVing Tuesday, Faculty and Staff Giving, and Student Giving initiatives. Manage the Pave the Way Brick Campaign, including donor engagement, order coordination, and stewardship activities. Partner with assigned colleges and university units to identify annual giving priorities and develop fundraising opportunities aligned with institutional goals. Assist with donor segmentation, campaign planning, and annual giving strategy development. Monitor annual giving performance metrics and recommend strategies to improve participation, donor retention, and fundraising results. Collaborate with the Operations and Communications teams to develop and implement annual giving communications, stewardship initiatives, and campaign materials. Provide leadership, oversight, and mentorship for Graduate Assistant involvement in student philanthropy initiatives. Perform other duties as assigned. Collaboration and Engagement (30%) Work collaboratively with colleagues across the Division of Alumni, Engagement and Philanthropy to support integrated fundraising initiatives. Represent Annual Giving at university events, alumni programs, donor engagement activities, and other fundraising events as appropriate. Coordinate stewardship and donor engagement opportunities that strengthen donor relationships and encourage continued philanthropic support. Assist with sponsorship and volunteer engagement opportunities connected to annual giving initiatives. Support special projects and other fundraising initiatives as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated ability to build and maintain meaningful donor and campus relationships. Strong organizational and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Knowledge of fundraising principles, donor stewardship, and annual giving best practices. Ability to analyze fundraising data and utilize reporting to inform strategy. Demonstrated initiative, sound judgment, and the ability to work independently and collaboratively. Commitment to confidentiality, professionalism, and exceptional customer service. Proficiency with CRM databases and Microsoft Office applications. Minimum Requirements Minimum of a Bachelor's degree. A minimum of one year of experience in fundraising, advancement, sales, marketing, business development, higher education, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to work with a variety of stakeholders to achieve common goals and objectives. Ability to work occasional evenings, weekends, and travel as required for fundraising and university events. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education, higher education advancement, or nonprofit fundraising. Experience managing fundraising campaigns and donor engagement initiatives. Knowledge of Blackbaud CRM or comparable fundraising databases. Physical Requirements Sedentary Work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/360": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Athletics, Sports Nutrition",
      "description": "Category: Athletic Coaching, Training and Program Management JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Position is responsible for the leadership and development of nutritional programs for over 350 student-athletes including design, implementation, and evaluation of nutrition and health programs to maximize athletic performance and the overall well-being of the whole person. The Director of Sports Nutrition will assist in providing our students with an exceptional student-athlete experience. This position will ensure our nutrition department is student-athlete focused and operating with integrity. Position is responsible for the leadership and development of nutritional programs for over 350 student-athletes including design, implementation, and evaluation of nutrition and health programs to maximize athletic performance and the overall well-being of the whole person. The Director of Sports Nutrition will assist in providing our students with an exceptional student-athlete experience. This position will ensure our nutrition department is student-athlete focused and operating with integrity. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Develop, lead, and manage effective programs to maximize the nutritional health and sports performance of all student-athletes. Develop and provide strategies that will enhance student-athlete performance, reduce the risk of fatigue and injury, and increase the motivation to continue with healthy nutritional habits. Working in collaboration with our mental health team, provide psychoeducation to student athletes and coaches. Conduct individual sessions, feedback assessment and training, comprehensive nutrition focused assessments for both the student-athlete and team. Maintain required certifications. Collaborate with the Integrated Healthcare Team to further support holistic model and enhance student-athlete experience. Ensure documentation and compliance with dietary plans, assessments and progress. Provide brief interventions and counseling to address a range of health and wellness issues, which may result in providing resources and referring individuals to professionals to assist with confidential and sensitive matters. Participate in the collection and analysis of tactical and statistical data and assist in designing plans and strategies. Identify and offer solutions to complex problems that may impact the overall performance of student-athletes and ultimately, the team. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to provide ideas, strategies, and leadership to implement change and ensure effective stakeholder collaboration. Ability to demonstrate knowledge of eating disorders and ability to effectively implement interventions to reduce the frequency, intensity, and duration of presenting symptoms. Support and lead initiatives that enhance student-athlete performance, retention, and life-long success. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree in Nutrition or related field. Registered dietitian by the commission on dietetic registration ( CDR ) and licensed dietitian (per state requirements) Previous experience working in collegiate or professional sports. Physical Requirements Sedentary Work: Capable of exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/354": {
      "title": "HVAC Technician",
      "description": "Category: Facilities Maintenance, Planning, Engineering, and Construction JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The HVAC Technician is responsible for performing inspections, servicing, and repair to heating, cooling, ventilating and refrigeration equipment. The HVAC Technician is responsible for performing inspections, servicing, and repair to heating, cooling, ventilating and refrigeration equipment. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Install, inspect, troubleshoot and repair HVAC equipment to include the following: central air conditioning systems, heat pumps, wall heaters, central heating systems, portable heaters, air flow ducting, walk-in coolers, freezers and all hydronic equipment. -Troubleshoot and repair HVAC equipment, control circuitry and refrigerant circuitry. -Maintain accurate maintenance records on equipment. -Perform preventative maintenance on commercial equipment. -Serve as boiler operator as needed. -Must wear proper PPE (safety shoes, hearing and eye protection)as required. -Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities -Ability to communicate effectively and appropriately. -Ability to interact in an effective and appropriate manner with diverse populations, the University community and the public. -Ability to handle multiple tasks simultaneously. -Ability to successfully complete assignments using appropriate methods, materials, tools and equipment in maintenance work as described above. -Ability to recognize occupational hazards and take appropriate safety precautions. -Ability to follow instructions. -Ability to drive light motor vehicle. -Ability to maintain accurate records. -Ability to perform light to heavy manual labor for extended periods of time under some unfavorable climatic conditions. -Ability to work overtime as required. -Ability to work in an on-call capacity and inclement weather duties. Required Minimum Qualifications -High school diploma -A minimum of two (2) year of commercial HVAC experience. -Refrigerant-handling certification. -Valid driver’s license. Physical Requirements -Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. -Bending, twisting and lifting weights to 100lbs. -Heights and working on elevations of 60 feet. -Work off ladders and lifts. "
