      "title": "Part-time Instructor (Pool) - Teaching & Learning",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Department of Teaching and Learning at Austin Peay State University is seeking qualified part-time Instructors to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the areas of instructional planning, assessment, and classroom management. The Department of Teaching and Learning at Austin Peay State University is seeking qualified part-time Instructors to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the areas of instructional planning, assessment, and classroom management. Primary Duties and Responsibilities - Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the areas of instructional planning, assessment, and classroom management. – Must be willing to teach at times and locations that best suits the needs of students and the Department. Physical Requirements Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Required Minimum Qualifications - A minimum of a Master’s Degree from an accredited university in the field of Education. – Three years of prior teaching experience in P – 12 public or private schools. – Hold a current state teaching license. – Must have the ability to learn or have prior experience with on-line teaching. – A background search will be required of the successful applicant. Required Documents 1. Cover Letter 2. Unofficial Transcript 3. Letter of Recommendation 1 4. Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents 1. Letter of Recommendation 2 2. Letter of Recommendation 3 The number of adjunct instructors hired varies from semester to semester, depending upon the needs of the department. Each applicant must include the names and contact information for three references, one of which must be from your most recent or current employer, with your application materials. Many people add this to the end of the CV/Resume. If you would like to additionally at