    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/352": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Employer Engagement",
      "description": "JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Assistant Director of Employer Engagement reports directly to the Executive Director of the Career Success Center within the Career Success Center at Austin Peay State University. This role supports the strategic development, coordination, and growth of employer partnerships, recruitment initiatives, and experiential learning opportunities that advance student career success and career readiness at APSU. The Assistant Director of Employer Engagement will serve as a collaborative, relationship-oriented, and student-centered professional who thrives in a fast-paced environment and is passionate about strengthening employer partnerships and advancing positive student career outcomes. Characteristics of a Successful Candidate Strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills with the ability to engage effectively with employers, students, faculty, staff, and community stakeholders. Highly organized with strong attention to detail and event coordination abilities. Demonstrated customer service mindset and professionalism. Ability to manage multiple projects, deadlines, and stakeholder relationships simultaneously. Strong communication, presentation, and outreach skills. Initiative-driven, collaborative, and solutions-oriented. Familiarity with career management platforms (e.g., Handshake) and employer engagement strategies. Responsibilities include: Employer Engagement & Partnership Development Develop, cultivate, and sustain relationships with local, regional, and national employers, alumni, and community partners to increase recruitment, internship, experiential learning, and employment opportunities for APSU students and alumni. Conduct employer outreach efforts through meetings, calls, presentations, networking events, campus visits, and employer site visits. Attend Chamber of Commerce events, Clarksville Industrial Association meetings, workforce development initiatives, and other networking opportunities to represent APSU and expand employer partnerships. Serve as a primary point of contact for employers regarding recruitment activities, event participation, and campus engagement opportunities. Support employer onboarding, engagement, and recruitment activities through Handshake. Collaborate with employers to identify hiring needs and align opportunities with student populations, academic programs, and workforce trends. Assist in expanding partnerships across various industry sectors through relationship-building and strategic engagement efforts. Collaborate with the Executive Director of the Career Success Center to support the establishment and sustainability of an Employer Advisory Council. Support strategic employer engagement initiatives designed to increase employer retention, recruitment activity, and workforce partnerships. Coordinate and oversee the Summer Internship Program logistics and execution with support from the Career Success Center team, while continuously strengthening partnerships with local Clarksville-Montgomery County employers. Collaborate with the Associate Director of Career Success Operations and Career Success Center team to coordinate and support logistics for career fairs and large-scale recruitment events. Coordinate networking events, employer panels, information sessions, tabling events, recruitment initiatives, and employer site visits. Collaborate with campus partners, vendors, facilities, and stakeholders to support successful employer engagement programming and recruitment events. Manage employer communications, registration processes, marketing coordination, and event follow-up efforts. Support the development and implementation of innovative employer engagement programming that enhances student access to career opportunities and industry connections. Provide coordination and operational support for experiential learning initiatives, internship programs, and workforce development events. Career Fairs, Recruitment Events & Programming Student & Campus Engagement Collaborate with career success coaches and campus partners to promote employer opportunities and career-related events to students. Support classroom presentations, workshops, and outreach initiatives related to career success resources, internships, networking, and employer engagement. Assist employers with navigating Handshake and recruitment processes, in collaboration with the Associate Director of Career Operations. Partner with career success coaches, academic departments, campus stakeholders to identify employer engagement opportunities aligned with academic programs and workforce trends. Promote employer participation in career readiness initiatives and student development programs. Support the supervision, training, and development of the Career Ambassador Program, particularly in areas related to employer engagement and outreach initiatives. Collaborate with the Associate Director of Career Success Operations and Career Success Center team to coordinate and support logistics for career fairs and large-scale recruitment events. Coordinate networking events, employer panels, information sessions, tabling events, recruitment initiatives, and employer site visits. Collaborate with campus partners, vendors, facilities, and stakeholders to support successful employer engagement programming and recruitment events. Manage employer communications, registration processes, marketing coordination, and event follow-up efforts. Support the development and implementation of innovative employer engagement programming that enhances student access to career opportunities and industry connections. Provide coordination and operational support for experiential learning initiatives, internship programs, and workforce development events Data, Reporting & Technology Platforms Utilize Handshake and related platforms to maintain accurate employer records, manage event registrations, track employer engagement, and support reporting efforts. Assist with collecting and analyzing employer engagement, recruitment activity, internship participation, and student employment data. Support assessment and reporting efforts related to employer partnerships, recruitment outcomes, and Career Success Center engagement metrics. Maintain organized records, communications, and tracking systems related to employer outreach and engagement efforts. Department and Division Maintain open communication with the Executive Director of the Career Success Center to share updates, opportunities, challenges, and recommendations. Represent the Career Success Center at university-wide events, community meetings, employer functions, and professional associations as needed. Stay informed on employer engagement trends, recruitment practices, and workforce development initiatives. Participate in professional development opportunities and related professional organizations. Assist with marketing, outreach, and promotional initiatives for career-related events and services. Work occasional evenings and weekends for employer events, career fairs, and university initiatives. Other duties as assigned. Required Skills and Qualifications Master’s degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Business, Communication, Human Resources, or a related field, and at least two (2) years of experience in employer engagement, career services, recruiting, workforce development, sales, business relations, or related field (Any appropriate combination of relevant education, full-time or graduate assistantship experience, and/or certifications may be considered). Advanced verbal and written communication skills, including presentation and relationship management experience. Strong organizational and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team-oriented environment. Demonstrated customer service and relationship-building skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Outlook, Word, PowerPoint, Excel) and operating a personal computer. Ability to engage professionally with diverse stakeholders including students, employers, faculty, staff, and community partners. Preferred Skills and Qualifications Master’s degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Business, Communication, Human Resources, or a related field, and at least five (5) years of experience in employer engagement, career services, recruiting, workforce development, sales, business relations, or related field (Any appropriate combination of relevant education, full-time or graduate assistantship experience, and/or certifications may be considered). Demonstrated ability to supervise, mentor, and develop staff and student leaders. Experience coordinating events, employer relations, or recruitment initiatives in higher education, nonprofit, or corporate settings. Experience using career management platforms such as Handshake. Knowledge of career readiness competencies, recruitment trends, and workforce development practices. Physical Requirements -Sedentary Work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/440": {
      "title": "Career Success Coach",
      "description": "Category: Student Support, Advising, and Career Development JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Career Success Coach reports to the Director of Career Development and plays a pivotal role in guiding students and alumni in their career development journey. This role provides comprehensive career coaching, delivers career readiness programming, and builds strategic relationships with employers and campus partners to enhance student career outcomes. This Career Success Coach role will be designated to serve the College of Arts & Letters and College of Education students, while collaborating with faculty and staff to integrate career readiness into the student experience at Austin Peay State University. The Career Success Coach will serve in a student-centered capacity to help students explore career pathways, develop career readiness skills, engage in experiential learning opportunities, and gain the skills and confidence needed for professional success. The Career Success Coach reports to the Director of Career Development and plays a pivotal role in guiding students and alumni in their career development journey. This role provides comprehensive career coaching, delivers career readiness programming, and builds strategic relationships with employers and campus partners to enhance student career outcomes. This Career Success Coach role will be designated to serve the College of Arts & Letters and College of Education students, while collaborating with faculty and staff to integrate career readiness into the student experience at Austin Peay State University. The Career Success Coach will serve in a student-centered capacity to help students explore career pathways, develop career readiness skills, engage in experiential learning opportunities, and gain the skills and confidence needed for professional success. Characteristics of a successful candidate: Integrity, kindness, creativity, and decisiveness. Passion for student success and career readiness. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to engage and inspire others. Desire to collaborate with faculty, employers, and campus partners. Demonstrated organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple priorities. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Career Coaching & Development Provide individual and group career coaching for students (undergraduate and graduate) and alumni exploring careers, navigating the job/internship search process, and preparing to transition from college to career, with a focus on College of Arts & Letters and College of Education students. Meet with students and alumni to assist with resume and cover letter development, practice interviews, graduate school planning, and other career-related topics. Discuss and interpret career assessments to support students in making informed decisions regarding majors and careers. Guide students and alumni in utilizing Handshake and other career platforms to support their career development goals. Campus Partnerships & Programming Plan, design and facilitate career workshops/programming, classroom presentations, and professional development training for students and campus partners, including career events tailored to the College of Arts & Letters and College of Education. Collaborate with faculty, academic departments, and student organizations to integrate career readiness initiatives into curriculum, co-curricular activities, and extracurricular programs. Support career events, including career fairs, networking events, and employer engagement activities. Attend regular meetings with the College of Arts & Letters and College of Education faculty/staff and leadership team, contributing to college-wide strategic planning. Employer Engagement & Industry Connections Network and maintain relationships with employers and alumni to support employer relations efforts, expanding career opportunities for students. Serve as a liaison between designated academic departments and employers to promote career opportunities to students and stay informed on hiring needs and industry trends. Data Analysis, Reporting & Technology Platforms Utilize Handshake and other online platforms to maintain accurate and current records, track student engagement, and support the day-to-day operations of the center. Contribute to the assessment and reporting of career services, student engagement, experiential learning, and post-graduate outcomes. Department and Division Maintain open communications with the Director of Career Development, the Career Success Center team, and College of Arts & Letters and College of Education leadership team to share information and engage in creative problem-solving to benefit the University community. Represent the Career Success Center at university-wide events, committees, and initiatives, as needed. Stay informed on career development best practices and employment trends. Participate in related professional organizations for continuing development. Provide general support for marketing and outreach efforts. Work occasional evenings and weekends for career-related events. Other duties as assigned. Required Skills and Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and related experience. Advanced verbal and written communication skills, including presentation experience. Demonstrated ability to provide coaching, advising, and mentoring to others. Exceptional organizational and time management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team setting. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Outlook, Word, PowerPoint, Excel) and operating a personal computer. Preferred Skills and Qualifications: Master’s degree in Higher Education, College Student Affairs Counseling, Education, Communication, Business, or a related field, and at least two (2) years of experience in career services, student advising, or a related field in higher education or industry (Any appropriate combination of relevant education, full-time or graduate assistantship experience, and/or certifications may be considered). Knowledge of career and student development frameworks and best practices, including NACE competencies. Experience using career management platforms such as Handshake. Interest in engaging with employers and developing strategic partnerships. Interest in working specifically with College of Arts & Letters and College of Education students. Physical Requirements Sedentary Work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/441": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Category: Student Support, Advising, and Career Development JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States Academic Advising and Student Success, formerly University Student Success, offers programs, services, and interactions that guide students in making informed and timely decisions to achieve their academic, career, and personal goals. The Academic Advisor reports to a designated College Student Success Director and plays a key role in supporting the success and retention of freshman and sophomore students. Advisors serve students within specific academic programs and collaborate with colleagues on their College Success Team. In addition, Academic Advisors will contribute to university-wide initiatives that foster student engagement, success, and student persistence across the APSU campus community. Academic Advising and Student Success, formerly University Student Success, offers programs, services, and interactions that guide students in making informed and timely decisions to achieve their academic, career, and personal goals. The Academic Advisor reports to a designated College Student Success Director and plays a key role in supporting the success and retention of freshman and sophomore students. Advisors serve students within specific academic programs and collaborate with colleagues on their College Success Team. In addition, Academic Advisors will contribute to university-wide initiatives that foster student engagement, success, and student persistence across the APSU campus community. Primary Duties and Responsibilities • Be a proactive and constructive participant within an advising team dedicated to student success. • Advise a caseload of freshmen and sophomore students to support their transition and success at APSU. • Provide proactive advising using techniques such as motivational interviewing and appreciative advising framework. • Support student retention by working with advisees in academic difficulty and recommending appropriate actions and resources. • Utilize retention data to inform decisions on student advising initiatives. • Track and manage student appointments, alerts, and notifications within EAB Navigate. • Assist students in the process of declaring or changing a major. • Participate in retention initiatives sponsored by the department, college, or university. • Help students understand university and degree requirements, interpret a degree evaluation, and develop a responsible approach to academic planning. • Be knowledgeable of all academic programs at the university; maintain awareness of and integrate revisions in departmental requirements. • Support the Student Success Director in planning the logistics and the advisement of students at Governors Orientation (GO). • Assist with the coordination and delivery of workshops and classroom presentations regarding academic advisement. • Represent the office during campus events such as Preview Day, First Fridays, and campus college fairs. • Assist the Executive Director in establishing student learning objectives related to the work of the department, intervene with students to produce intended outcomes and participate in assessment and evaluation. • Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Ability to efficiently operate a personal computer and associated software (Outlook, Word, Excel, etc.), SungardHE Banner and EAB Navigate. • Knowledge of university and degree requirements. • Ability to maintain accurate files and records of student contacts, both electronically and on paper. • Ability to maintain confidentiality. • Ability to communicate effectively and appropriately, both verbally and in writing. • Ability to work in a team environment as well as complete tasks individually. • Ability to apply student development and career development theories. • Commitment to keeping abreast of current academic advising and student success literature and practices. Minimum Requirements • Bachelor’s degree from an accredited university • Experience working in an educational and/or university setting with college student populations. • Computer literacy. • Ability to work flexible hours to include evenings and weekends. • Knowledgeable about FERPA. • Experience working with various populations. • A background check will be required for the successful applicant. Physical Requirements -Sedentary Work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. "
    },
    "https://ibqzjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/443": {
      "title": "Specialist, Instructional Technology",
      "description": "Category: Academic Program Management and Instructional Services JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Clarksville, TN, United States The Instructional Technology Specialist (ITS) reports to the Director, Instructional Technology for Distance Education, and provides direct support to faculty, staff, and students who use Distance Education-managed technologies for teaching and learning. This position is responsible for initiatives in user support, resource and training development, marketing and communication, and assessment. The ITS will also assist with the management of instructional technology. Distance Education’s instructional technologies include the learning management system, similarity and AI writing detection, online proctoring, digital accessibility, and media management. The Instructional Technology Specialist (ITS) reports to the Director, Instructional Technology for Distance Education, and provides direct support to faculty, staff, and students who use Distance Education-managed technologies for teaching and learning. This position is responsible for initiatives in user support, resource and training development, marketing and communication, and assessment. The ITS will also assist with the management of instructional technology. Distance Education’s instructional technologies include the learning management system, similarity and AI writing detection, online proctoring, digital accessibility, and media management. Primary Responsibilities and Duties Provide direct support and troubleshooting to instructional technology users via phone, tickets, email, and in-person. Maintain accurate records of requests, incidents, and resolutions using a ticketing system. Deliver excellent customer service, build positive relationships, and communicate effectively with vendors, faculty, staff, and students of varying technical skills. Design and present instructional technology training. Create and maintain standard operating procedures, resources, media, web pages, and other materials. Develop informative and engaging marketing materials and communications to promote Distance Education initiatives. This includes regularly sharing information about events, resources, technological features, and other topics through social media, newsletters, announcements, website updates, and other channels. Track and resolve vendor and instructional technology performance issues to support contract monitoring. Collect and analyze data from reporting, tech tool usage, contract monitoring, tool audits, user feedback, etc., to make informed decisions. Identify and lead opportunities for continuous improvement, collaboration, and proactive initiatives regarding Distance Education’s instructional technology. Stay current with emerging technologies and trends in Distance Education to inform decision-making and support innovative teaching and learning best practices. Assist with the supervision and training of the Distance Education support desk student technicians. Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of instructional technologies and learning management systems (LMS). Technical troubleshooting skills, including familiarity with Windows and Mac OS, web browsers, mobile devices, webcams, and microphones. A customer-centric mindset, with a focus on providing excellent service and support. Strong communication and interpersonal skills to interact effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds and technical skill levels. Ability to effectively manage and accomplish tasks while working within a team-oriented environment toward collective goals. Problem-solving and decision-making skills and the ability to implement effective and timely solutions. Ability to recognize challenges and opportunities and take initiative to address them. Navigate multiple tasks simultaneously while meeting deadlines. Maintain confidentiality of records and information. Ability to occasionally work a flexible schedule and varied hours. Required Minimum Qualifications Minimum of a Bachelor’s Degree conferred upon hire date. Experience in software support, technology training, customer service support, or relevant field. Physical Requirements Sedentary Work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects. "
    }
